_url":"https://github.com/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commit/0e06a804cf5535b52d255afeba49cd1f3725febe","sha":"0e06a804cf5535b52d255afeba49cd1f3725febe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commits/0e06a804cf5535b52d255afeba49cd1f3725febe"}],"sha":"47a4ce481c1234415c8663161a3d29c2c1ad576e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commits/47a4ce481c1234415c8663161a3d29c2c1ad576e"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commits/0e06a804cf5535b52d255afeba49cd1f3725febe/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-11T18:37:43Z","email":"mcroker@gmail.com","name":"Martin Croker"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-11T18:37:43Z","email":"mcroker@gmail.com","name":"Martin Croker"},"message":"Document remote-loading integrity in architecture/poc docs, prune stale TODOs\n\narchitecture.md/poc-writeup.md hadn''t caught up with the 08-11 signed-\nmanifest work (trust registry, two-stage verify). Also removes 4 TODO\nitems confirmed resolved by checking live state: shared-ui-scds-core/\nshared-federation-runtime now match platform-versions.json everywhere,\nmfe-pot-platform''s ci.yml landed, shared-platform-standards published\n0.2.0 (confirming its Actions-access grant holds), and Grafana''s EKS\nIngress already has TLS.","tree":{"sha":"889a4df79069bcdce2471eb1313f45368d7aaad0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/git/trees/889a4df79069bcdce2471eb1313f45368d7aaad0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/git/commits/0e06a804cf5535b52d255afeba49cd1f3725febe","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commit/0e06a804cf5535b52d255afeba49cd1f3725febe","node_id":"C_kwDOTqlj_toAKDBlMDZhODA0Y2Y1NTM1YjUyZDI1NWFmZWJhNDljZDFmMzcyNWZlYmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commit/b5176590fff9e72bc7388f101c93ef481e02d689","sha":"b5176590fff9e72bc7388f101c93ef481e02d689","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commits/b5176590fff9e72bc7388f101c93ef481e02d689"}],"sha":"0e06a804cf5535b52d255afeba49cd1f3725febe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commits/0e06a804cf5535b52d255afeba49cd1f3725febe"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commits/b5176590fff9e72bc7388f101c93ef481e02d689/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-11T17:39:33Z","email":"mcroker@gmail.com","name":"Martin Croker"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-11T17:39:33Z","email":"mcroker@gmail.com","name":"Martin Croker"},"message":"Mark federation remote-loading integrity done, rewrite design doc\n\nBoth Phase 1 (job-bank-mfe/job-bank-shell) and Phase 2 (the other 3\nremotes + msca-shell) are implemented and confirmed green on real kind\ndeployments across all 7 repos. Rewrites the design doc post-implementation\nto describe what was actually built -- the original two-tier sketch\n(self-published hash for first-party remotes, signed manifest for\nhypothetical third-party ones) didn''t survive contact with its own threat\nmodel, corrected during implementation to one signature mechanism for\nevery remote, with \"tier\" surviving only as a property of how a trust-\nregistry entry gets provisioned.","tree":{"sha":"9ee96251363665f23da86bed8fd1ba0932770ab3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/git/trees/9ee96251363665f23da86bed8fd1ba0932770ab3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/git/commits/b5176590fff9e72bc7388f101c93ef481e02d689","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commit/b5176590fff9e72bc7388f101c93ef481e02d689","node_id":"C_kwDOTqlj_toAKGI1MTc2NTkwZmZmOWU3MmJjNzM4OGYxMDFjOTNlZjQ4MWUwMmQ2ODk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commit/c97c2f93ccc5fe72e65d5d85794422573acf6a36","sha":"c97c2f93ccc5fe72e65d5d85794422573acf6a36","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commits/c97c2f93ccc5fe72e65d5d85794422573acf6a36"}],"sha":"b5176590fff9e72bc7388f101c93ef481e02d689","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commits/b5176590fff9e72bc7388f101c93ef481e02d689"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commits/c97c2f93ccc5fe72e65d5d85794422573acf6a36/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-11T14:37:41Z","email":"mcroker@gmail.com","name":"Martin Croker"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-11T14:37:41Z","email":"mcroker@gmail.com","name":"Martin Croker"},"message":"Broaden federation remote-loading integrity design to a two-tier trust model\n\nTier 1 (self-published SHA-384, the original 2026-08-10 scope) only closes\nthe gap for remotes we build ourselves -- a malicious third-party remote\nwould just hash its own payload correctly. Tier 2 adds a platform-owned\ntrust registry + signed manifests for remotes built by providers outside\nthis family''s control, since the architecture already supports composing\nruntime-loaded remotes we didn''t build.","tree":{"sha":"96e677219ac34f047255e670aa3c368e30f23600","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/git/trees/96e677219ac34f047255e670aa3c368e30f23600"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/git/commits/c97c2f93ccc5fe72e65d5d85794422573acf6a36","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commit/c97c2f93ccc5fe72e65d5d85794422573acf6a36","node_id":"C_kwDOTqlj_toAKGM5N2MyZjkzY2NjNWZlNzJlNjVkNWQ4NTc5NDQyMjU3M2FjZjZhMzY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commit/a7d7d662a34de75ca037d239800c43cf652af2c1","sha":"a7d7d662a34de75ca037d239800c43cf652af2c1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commits/a7d7d662a34de75ca037d239800c43cf652af2c1"}],"sha":"c97c2f93ccc5fe72e65d5d85794422573acf6a36","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commits/c97c2f93ccc5fe72e65d5d85794422573acf6a36"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commits/a7d7d662a34de75ca037d239800c43cf652af2c1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-11T14:31:16Z","email":"mcroker@gmail.com","name":"Martin Croker"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-11T14:31:16Z","email":"mcroker@gmail.com","name":"Martin Croker"},"message":"Add tools/build-all.sh, document deploy-eks.sh''s new redeploy-only default\n\nEvery repo''s deploy-eks workflow now defaults its workflow_dispatch trigger\nto skip_build=true (deploy the already-published image, no rebuild) --\nbuild-all.sh is the new counterpart, passing skip_build=false to force a\nfresh build+publish across all 7 repos without touching any live cluster.","tree":{"sha":"6922c02311fdecc9110b69ef8f6d565b320cafc1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/git/trees/6922c02311fdecc9110b69ef8f6d565b320cafc1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/git/commits/a7d7d662a34de75ca037d239800c43cf652af2c1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commit/a7d7d662a34de75ca037d239800c43cf652af2c1","node_id":"C_kwDOTqlj_toAKGE3ZDdkNjYyYTM0ZGU3NWNhMDM3ZDIzOTgwMGM0M2NmNjUyYWYyYzE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commit/28059f689f4b71a8cb69123d43081050c04fb874","sha":"28059f689f4b71a8cb69123d43081050c04fb874","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commits/28059f689f4b71a8cb69123d43081050c04fb874"}],"sha":"a7d7d662a34de75ca037d239800c43cf652af2c1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commits/a7d7d662a34de75ca037d239800c43cf652af2c1"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commits/28059f689f4b71a8cb69123d43081050c04fb874/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-11T10:40:12Z","email":"mcroker@gmail.com","name":"Martin Croker"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-11T10:40:12Z","email":"mcroker@gmail.com","name":"Martin Croker"},"message":"deploy-eks.sh: accept 302 in Step 6 host check, fix 000/000000 double-echo\n\ncms and grafana both redirect \"/\" (Strapi admin login, Grafana login page)\n-- a 302 there proves TLS+DNS+routing worked just as much as the existing\n200/404 cases, but the check only accepted those two and flagged both as\nfailures. Also: on a genuine connection failure curl already prints its\nown \"000\" http_code via -w before exiting non-zero, so the old\n`|| echo 000` fallback double-appended into a confusing \"000000\".","tree":{"sha":"c328b8aa965acbc86f6e0cd88287033dd1a3c257","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/git/trees/c328b8aa965acbc86f6e0cd88287033dd1a3c257"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/git/commits/28059f689f4b71a8cb69123d43081050c04fb874","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commit/28059f689f4b71a8cb69123d43081050c04fb874","node_id":"C_kwDOTqlj_toAKDI4MDU5ZjY4OWY0YjcxYThjYjY5MTIzZDQzMDgxMDUwYzA0ZmI4NzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commit/063d423d227c8c8e8ffcb680b462e4a56ba6de5c","sha":"063d423d227c8c8e8ffcb680b462e4a56ba6de5c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commits/063d423d227c8c8e8ffcb680b462e4a56ba6de5c"}],"sha":"28059f689f4b71a8cb69123d43081050c04fb874","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commits/28059f689f4b71a8cb69123d43081050c04fb874"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commits/063d423d227c8c8e8ffcb680b462e4a56ba6de5c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-10T22:02:16Z","email":"mcroker@gmail.com","name":"Martin Croker"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-10T22:02:16Z","email":"mcroker@gmail.com","name":"Martin Croker"},"message":"deploy-eks.sh: seed Unleash feature flags after hostname verification\n\nNew Step 7 calls mfe-pot-platform''s seed-unleash-flags.mjs against the real\nunleash.$DOMAIN_NAME hostname over https, deliberately placed after Step 6''s\nverification loop confirms DNS/TLS/routing already work -- a fresh\ncert-manager cert can take longer to become reachable than unleash''s own\nhelm --wait. Same script as deploy-local.sh''s kind path, just pointed at\nreal DNS instead of the localhost + Host-header trick kind needs.","tree":{"sha":"7248928f74484095fbfb1e21cd594f63d3f72f6c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/git/trees/7248928f74484095fbfb1e21cd594f63d3f72f6c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/git/commits/063d423d227c8c8e8ffcb680b462e4a56ba6de5c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commit/063d423d227c8c8e8ffcb680b462e4a56ba6de5c","node_id":"C_kwDOTqlj_toAKDA2M2Q0MjNkMjI3YzhjOGU4ZmZjYjY4MGI0NjJlNGE1NmJhNmRlNWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commit/0de3d90ee198afefd466ecc22bd1f4c810fd8ca4","sha":"0de3d90ee198afefd466ecc22bd1f4c810fd8ca4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commits/0de3d90ee198afefd466ecc22bd1f4c810fd8ca4"}],"sha":"063d423d227c8c8e8ffcb680b462e4a56ba6de5c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commits/063d423d227c8c8e8ffcb680b462e4a56ba6de5c"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commits/0de3d90ee198afefd466ecc22bd1f4c810fd8ca4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-10T14:14:45Z","email":"mcroker@gmail.com","name":"Martin Croker"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-10T14:14:45Z","email":"mcroker@gmail.com","name":"Martin Croker"},"message":"Prune completed items from TODO.md\n\nRemoves fully-done sections (ingress naming, second host app, Angular→React\nmigration, publish-shared-packages.yml fixes, design principles, sidebar\nnav scope) and strips checked-off items from mixed sections, keeping only\nstill-open work.","tree":{"sha":"05206e3e51cc50e644af86bd409652adff3d4b82","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/git/trees/05206e3e51cc50e644af86bd409652adff3d4b82"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/git/commits/0de3d90ee198afefd466ecc22bd1f4c810fd8ca4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commit/0de3d90ee198afefd466ecc22bd1f4c810fd8ca4","node_id":"C_kwDOTqlj_toAKDBkZTNkOTBlZTE5OGFmZWZkNDY2ZWNjMjJiZDFmNGM4MTBmZDhjYTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commit/c96df9b6de72a889a0007165613fcae9ddcece97","sha":"c96df9b6de72a889a0007165613fcae9ddcece97","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commits/c96df9b6de72a889a0007165613fcae9ddcece97"}],"sha":"0de3d90ee198afefd466ecc22bd1f4c810fd8ca4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commits/0de3d90ee198afefd466ecc22bd1f4c810fd8ca4"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commits/c96df9b6de72a889a0007165613fcae9ddcece97/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-10T11:41:30Z","email":"mcroker@gmail.com","name":"Martin Croker"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-10T11:41:30Z","email":"mcroker@gmail.com","name":"Martin Croker"},"message":"Add federation remote-loading integrity item to TODO\n\nShells fetch remote manifests from Strapi at runtime with no SRI/signature\ncheck before executing the fetched remoteEntry.json.","tree":{"sha":"3f1afb5b4744bed942a0019843bdbfae88b30340","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/git/trees/3f1afb5b4744bed942a0019843bdbfae88b30340"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/git/commits/c96df9b6de72a889a0007165613fcae9ddcece97","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commit/c96df9b6de72a889a0007165613fcae9ddcece97","node_id":"C_kwDOTqlj_toAKGM5NmRmOWI2ZGU3MmE4ODlhMDAwNzE2NTYxM2ZjYWU5ZGRjZWNlOTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commit/a7cba28fd07ae932c655a60152e53e370bada3fb","sha":"a7cba28fd07ae932c655a60152e53e370bada3fb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commits/a7cba28fd07ae932c655a60152e53e370bada3fb"}],"sha":"c96df9b6de72a889a0007165613fcae9ddcece97","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commits/c96df9b6de72a889a0007165613fcae9ddcece97"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commits/a7cba28fd07ae932c655a60152e53e370bada3fb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-10T11:06:33Z","email":"mcroker@gmail.com","name":"Martin Croker"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-10T11:06:33Z","email":"mcroker@gmail.com","name":"Martin Croker"},"message":"Document Unleash''s default admin login in local setup steps\n\ncharts/unleash only bootstraps its three API tokens on startup, not a\nUI password, so the admin UI falls back to Unleash''s own out-of-the-box\ndefault rather than anything this family sets -- worth calling out\nexplicitly since it reads as an omission next to the CMS line above it.","tree":{"sha":"f7fc120ab115836bf42622735136d84a4644677a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/git/trees/f7fc120ab115836bf42622735136d84a4644677a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/git/commits/a7cba28fd07ae932c655a60152e53e370bada3fb","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commit/a7cba28fd07ae932c655a60152e53e370bada3fb","node_id":"C_kwDOTqlj_toAKGE3Y2JhMjhmZDA3YWU5MzJjNjU1YTYwMTUyZTUzZTM3MGJhZGEzZmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commit/d7541be4cd9c57cbbd13228725bf023fb6b70fb8","sha":"d7541be4cd9c57cbbd13228725bf023fb6b70fb8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commits/d7541be4cd9c57cbbd13228725bf023fb6b70fb8"}],"sha":"a7cba28fd07ae932c655a60152e53e370bada3fb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commits/a7cba28fd07ae932c655a60152e53e370bada3fb"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commits/d7541be4cd9c57cbbd13228725bf023fb6b70fb8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-09T22:06:20Z","email":"mcroker@gmail.com","name":"Martin Croker"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-09T22:06:20Z","email":"mcroker@gmail.com","name":"Martin Croker"},"message":"Add living architecture doc, fix stale docs across the family\n\ndocs/architecture.md is a new non-dated system overview (topology,\nrequest flows, decision index) distinct from platform''s CLAUDE.md\n(rationale/gotchas) and docs/plans/ (dated history).\n\nREADME.md''s /etc/hosts list was missing unleash/otel/grafana, all three\nserving real content. CLAUDE.md''s deploy-local.sh description was\nmissing the Unleash and OTel-stack deploy steps.\n\npoc-writeup.md had drifted from the day''s second half of work: two\n\"proven\" claims (life-events'' schema-driven kit, dashboard-bff calling\nother BFFs for tracing) described mechanisms built *and abandoned* the\nsame day they were written up, replaced with plain composed pages and\nbrowser-mediated cross-domain composition respectively. Rewrote those,\nthen added the design-principles/resilience pass (zero-downtime\ndeploys, node-failure survival, Redis degradation, BFF-boundary\nenforcement, Unleash-backed A/B testing) as new decisions/proof points,\nincluding the EKS replicaCount revert as a real infra lesson.","tree":{"sha":"e84ac720a17919f78b593d941043f5c4c5615a74","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/git/trees/e84ac720a17919f78b593d941043f5c4c5615a74"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/git/commits/d7541be4cd9c57cbbd13228725bf023fb6b70fb8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commit/d7541be4cd9c57cbbd13228725bf023fb6b70fb8","node_id":"C_kwDOTqlj_toAKGQ3NTQxYmU0Y2Q5YzU3Y2JiZDEzMjI4NzI1YmYwMjNmYjZiNzBmYjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commit/e70a5f5630e40344c895ef5b9a1df3933acacff8","sha":"e70a5f5630e40344c895ef5b9a1df3933acacff8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commits/e70a5f5630e40344c895ef5b9a1df3933acacff8"}],"sha":"d7541be4cd9c57cbbd13228725bf023fb6b70fb8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commits/d7541be4cd9c57cbbd13228725bf023fb6b70fb8"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commits/e70a5f5630e40344c895ef5b9a1df3933acacff8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-09T18:13:23Z","email":"mcroker@gmail.com","name":"Martin Croker"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-09T18:13:23Z","email":"mcroker@gmail.com","name":"Martin Croker"},"message":"Sequence unleash into deploy scripts, close out design-principles TODOs\n\ndeploy-local.sh/deploy-eks.sh now deploy mfe-pot-platform''s new Unleash\nchart alongside session-cache/otel-collector. TODO.md''s \"Design\nprinciples\" section marked done with evidence for each of the 6\nprinciples -- see mfe-pot-platform/CLAUDE.md for the durable architecture\nreference.","tree":{"sha":"82c7a519d518085cc160566464b4aaa65f1130fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/git/trees/82c7a519d518085cc160566464b4aaa65f1130fc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/git/commits/e70a5f5630e40344c895ef5b9a1df3933acacff8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commit/e70a5f5630e40344c895ef5b9a1df3933acacff8","node_id":"C_kwDOTqlj_toAKGU3MGE1ZjU2MzBlNDAzNDRjODk1ZWY1YjlhMWRmMzkzM2FjYWNmZjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commit/8aef3b06764623cfd83f9b8fbc2fee1386c05366","sha":"8aef3b06764623cfd83f9b8fbc2fee1386c05366","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commits/8aef3b06764623cfd83f9b8fbc2fee1386c05366"}],"sha":"e70a5f5630e40344c895ef5b9a1df3933acacff8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commits/e70a5f5630e40344c895ef5b9a1df3933acacff8"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commits/8aef3b06764623cfd83f9b8fbc2fee1386c05366/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-09T12:40:01Z","email":"mcroker@gmail.com","name":"Martin Croker"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-09T12:40:01Z","email":"mcroker@gmail.com","name":"Martin Croker"},"message":"TODO: close msca-shell menu/Service-Canada-alignment item, add Strapi content-organization scoping\n\nMenu item done: mfe-pot-msca-shell''s sidebar now lists the real Service\nCanada program set (inert/\"coming soon\" where there''s no backing remote)\nplus a new bottom-of-sidebar Demo links section (Grafana/CMS/job-bank-shell).\n\nAlso records a new, separately-scoped item: Strapi''s page-content collection\nhas no app/kind structure today, making its admin list one long\nundifferentiated scroll -- design captured (two new enum fields, a\nkey-suffix heuristic for kind) but not yet implemented.","tree":{"sha":"3b90a4896922d97779811340e58ce567b6bc71fd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/git/trees/3b90a4896922d97779811340e58ce567b6bc71fd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/git/commits/8aef3b06764623cfd83f9b8fbc2fee1386c05366","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commit/8aef3b06764623cfd83f9b8fbc2fee1386c05366","node_id":"C_kwDOTqlj_toAKDhhZWYzYjA2NzY0NjIzY2ZkODNmOWI4ZmJjMmZlZTEzODZjMDUzNjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commit/7c3828c6a6a0f42db1e992573a4e156e04ccff2a","sha":"7c3828c6a6a0f42db1e992573a4e156e04ccff2a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commits/7c3828c6a6a0f42db1e992573a4e156e04ccff2a"}],"sha":"8aef3b06764623cfd83f9b8fbc2fee1386c05366","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commits/8aef3b06764623cfd83f9b8fbc2fee1386c05366"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commits/7c3828c6a6a0f42db1e992573a4e156e04ccff2a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-09T12:18:48Z","email":"mcroker@gmail.com","name":"Martin Croker"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-09T12:18:48Z","email":"mcroker@gmail.com","name":"Martin Croker"},"message":"Remove CMS-migration TODO for life-events checklist content -- resolved via i18n JSON instead\n\nmfe-pot-life-events-mfe''s checklist/service-link content now lives in\ni18n JSON as a deliberate resting state, not a stepping stone to CMS\nkeys -- no app in the family models a CMS key resolving to an array\nof items, only flat single-string keys.","tree":{"sha":"dd731452e53d40af34b17619148ddce02e3dfd67","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/git/trees/dd731452e53d40af34b17619148ddce02e3dfd67"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/git/commits/7c3828c6a6a0f42db1e992573a4e156e04ccff2a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commit/7c3828c6a6a0f42db1e992573a4e156e04ccff2a","node_id":"C_kwDOTqlj_toAKDdjMzgyOGM2YTZhMGY0MmRiMWU5OTI1NzNhNGUxNTZlMDRjY2ZmMmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commit/ed25810968a7b33da1d8892dc8c9af0b0b06dced","sha":"ed25810968a7b33da1d8892dc8c9af0b0b06dced","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commits/ed25810968a7b33da1d8892dc8c9af0b0b06dced"}],"sha":"7c3828c6a6a0f42db1e992573a4e156e04ccff2a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commits/7c3828c6a6a0f42db1e992573a4e156e04ccff2a"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commits/ed25810968a7b33da1d8892dc8c9af0b0b06dced/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-09T11:39:44Z","email":"mcroker@gmail.com","name":"Martin Croker"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-09T11:39:44Z","email":"mcroker@gmail.com","name":"Martin Croker"},"message":"Fix deploy-local.sh CLUSTER_NAME default mismatch, document single-app redeploy\n\nThe orchestrator defaulted CLUSTER_NAME to \"mfe-pot\" while every sibling\nrepo''s own tools/deploy-local.sh (and this README''s walkthrough) defaults\nto \"kind\" -- running the orchestrator then later redeploying one app\nstandalone silently targeted a second, disconnected cluster instead of\nupdating the shared one. Aligns the orchestrator to \"kind\" and documents\nboth entrypoints (the orchestrator''s skip-logic, and redeploying a single\nsibling in place) in the README.","tree":{"sha":"007defa69b7de1cce60e862b2a430150e3a311e0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/git/trees/007defa69b7de1cce60e862b2a430150e3a311e0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/git/commits/ed25810968a7b33da1d8892dc8c9af0b0b06dced","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commit/ed25810968a7b33da1d8892dc8c9af0b0b06dced","node_id":"C_kwDOTqlj_toAKGVkMjU4MTA5NjhhN2IzM2RhMWQ4ODkyZGM4YzlhZjBiMGIwNmRjZWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commit/735e499833db2fc3e7f27fb92f92b9afe65d6098","sha":"735e499833db2fc3e7f27fb92f92b9afe65d6098","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commits/735e499833db2fc3e7f27fb92f92b9afe65d6098"}],"sha":"ed25810968a7b33da1d8892dc8c9af0b0b06dced","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commits/ed25810968a7b33da1d8892dc8c9af0b0b06dced"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commits/735e499833db2fc3e7f27fb92f92b9afe65d6098/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-09T11:39:06Z","email":"mcroker@gmail.com","name":"Martin Croker"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-09T11:39:06Z","email":"mcroker@gmail.com","name":"Martin Croker"},"message":"TODO: close the browser-to-collector CORS gap in Observability\n\nCloses the \"browser leg\" gap flagged when BFF-to-BFF trace propagation\nlanded - a real browser session surfaced the predicted CORS preflight\nfailure, fixed in mfe-pot-platform''s otel-collector chart (see that\nrepo''s own commit).","tree":{"sha":"89e9d950e159455aae6a6545a76d7e37a3ab40e3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/git/trees/89e9d950e159455aae6a6545a76d7e37a3ab40e3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/git/commits/735e499833db2fc3e7f27fb92f92b9afe65d6098","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commit/735e499833db2fc3e7f27fb92f92b9afe65d6098","node_id":"C_kwDOTqlj_toAKDczNWU0OTk4MzNkYjJmYzNlN2YyN2ZiOTJmOTJiOWFmZTY1ZDYwOTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commit/06fec0519da7689f8b047a7c62541b09cc24a2f6","sha":"06fec0519da7689f8b047a7c62541b09cc24a2f6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commits/06fec0519da7689f8b047a7c62541b09cc24a2f6"}],"sha":"735e499833db2fc3e7f27fb92f92b9afe65d6098","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commits/735e499833db2fc3e7f27fb92f92b9afe65d6098"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commits/06fec0519da7689f8b047a7c62541b09cc24a2f6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-09T11:35:56Z","email":"mcroker@gmail.com","name":"Martin Croker"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-09T11:35:56Z","email":"mcroker@gmail.com","name":"Martin Croker"},"message":"Add life-events kit SCDS/shared-package promotion backlog item\n\nCaptures two deferred decisions from the life-events-mfe schema-to-page\nrefactor: promoting the duplicated card-grid CSS pattern (shared with\ndashboard-mfe''s Overview.tsx) into shared-ui-scds-core, and where the\nkit would need to move if life-events ever splits into separate repos.","tree":{"sha":"4430543f648c157febdadf7563ce66be71a81396","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/git/trees/4430543f648c157febdadf7563ce66be71a81396"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/git/commits/06fec0519da7689f8b047a7c62541b09cc24a2f6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commit/06fec0519da7689f8b047a7c62541b09cc24a2f6","node_id":"C_kwDOTqlj_toAKDA2ZmVjMDUxOWRhNzY4OWY4YjA0N2E3YzYyNTQxYjA5Y2MyNGEyZjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commit/c3091029222ba41d31dad0a6a3550232af4265fa","sha":"c3091029222ba41d31dad0a6a3550232af4265fa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commits/c3091029222ba41d31dad0a6a3550232af4265fa"}],"sha":"06fec0519da7689f8b047a7c62541b09cc24a2f6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commits/06fec0519da7689f8b047a7c62541b09cc24a2f6"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commits/c3091029222ba41d31dad0a6a3550232af4265fa/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-09T11:09:17Z","email":"mcroker@gmail.com","name":"Martin Croker"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-09T11:09:17Z","email":"mcroker@gmail.com","name":"Martin Croker"},"message":"deploy-eks.sh: install kube-state-metrics alongside the observability stack\n\nMatches mfe-pot-platform''s identical addition to its own\ntools/deploy-local.sh -- inserted between tempo and prometheus so the\nService exists before Prometheus''s scrape config targets it, plus the\nsame kubectl rollout restart fix after the prometheus helm upgrade (its\nDeployment has no ConfigMap-checksum annotation, so a scrape-config-only\nchange never restarted the pod on its own).","tree":{"sha":"1843c4fa9ccad555986c8c807568a1245e81cfe4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/git/trees/1843c4fa9ccad555986c8c807568a1245e81cfe4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/git/commits/c3091029222ba41d31dad0a6a3550232af4265fa","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commit/c3091029222ba41d31dad0a6a3550232af4265fa","node_id":"C_kwDOTqlj_toAKGMzMDkxMDI5MjIyYmE0MWQzMWRhZDBhNmEzNTUwMjMyYWY0MjY1ZmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commit/c9393eaa299c3e1112e4c1757070182c51e466ef","sha":"c9393eaa299c3e1112e4c1757070182c51e466ef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commits/c9393eaa299c3e1112e4c1757070182c51e466ef"}],"sha":"c3091029222ba41d31dad0a6a3550232af4265fa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commits/c3091029222ba41d31dad0a6a3550232af4265fa"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commits/c9393eaa299c3e1112e4c1757070182c51e466ef/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-09T11:02:27Z","email":"mcroker@gmail.com","name":"Martin Croker"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-09T11:02:27Z","email":"mcroker@gmail.com","name":"Martin Croker"},"message":"Add TODO: put Grafana''s public Ingress on HTTPS like every other service\n\nGrafana''s Ingress currently serves plain HTTP while every other public\nIngress host in the family terminates TLS via cert-manager.","tree":{"sha":"90c7211db0b07399253d5153697405e8e24f187c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/git/trees/90c7211db0b07399253d5153697405e8e24f187c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/git/commits/c9393eaa299c3e1112e4c1757070182c51e466ef","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commit/c9393eaa299c3e1112e4c1757070182c51e466ef","node_id":"C_kwDOTqlj_toAKGM5MzkzZWFhMjk5YzNlMTExMmU0YzE3NTcwNzAxODJjNTFlNDY2ZWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commit/c375d1752c0d00b5e0a96793e1b3cc70f6be7090","sha":"c375d1752c0d00b5e0a96793e1b3cc70f6be7090","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commits/c375d1752c0d00b5e0a96793e1b3cc70f6be7090"}],"sha":"c9393eaa299c3e1112e4c1757070182c51e466ef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commits/c9393eaa299c3e1112e4c1757070182c51e466ef"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commits/c375d1752c0d00b5e0a96793e1b3cc70f6be7090/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-09T10:53:43Z","email":"mcroker@gmail.com","name":"Martin Croker"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-09T10:53:43Z","email":"mcroker@gmail.com","name":"Martin Croker"},"message":"Add tools/kctx.sh: show/switch which cluster kubectl points at\n\nkind and EKS contexts commonly coexist in the same kubeconfig, and\nrunning commands against the wrong one is an easy mistake. Defaults to\nper-shell switching (via a layered KUBECONFIG override) so one terminal\ncan stay on kind while another points at EKS; --global falls back to\nmutating ~/.kube/config''s current-context for every shell.","tree":{"sha":"f7515785a693873d9e02f4bb53a25bfbacbbade0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/git/trees/f7515785a693873d9e02f4bb53a25bfbacbbade0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/git/commits/c375d1752c0d00b5e0a96793e1b3cc70f6be7090","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commit/c375d1752c0d00b5e0a96793e1b3cc70f6be7090","node_id":"C_kwDOTqlj_toAKGMzNzVkMTc1MmMwZDAwYjVlMGE5Njc5M2UxYjNjYzcwZjZiZTcwOTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commit/78879d53b6d960ef17fb4f22a386d52ece00a468","sha":"78879d53b6d960ef17fb4f22a386d52ece00a468","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commits/78879d53b6d960ef17fb4f22a386d52ece00a468"}],"sha":"c375d1752c0d00b5e0a96793e1b3cc70f6be7090","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commits/c375d1752c0d00b5e0a96793e1b3cc70f6be7090"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commits/78879d53b6d960ef17fb4f22a386d52ece00a468/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-09T09:59:47Z","email":"mcroker@gmail.com","name":"Martin Croker"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-09T09:59:47Z","email":"mcroker@gmail.com","name":"Martin Croker"},"message":"Track life-events-mfe''s journey.* i18n-to-CMS migration as a backlog item\n\nDeferred during the Strapi content-decentralization work across the app\nrepos -- the journey.* step-narrative content is inconsistent with each\nlife event''s CMS-driven intro block, but migrating it was explicitly out\nof scope for that pass.","tree":{"sha":"d8929c1f6ee821c223948f961b34cc2dff615f13","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/git/trees/d8929c1f6ee821c223948f961b34cc2dff615f13"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/git/commits/78879d53b6d960ef17fb4f22a386d52ece00a468","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commit/78879d53b6d960ef17fb4f22a386d52ece00a468","node_id":"C_kwDOTqlj_toAKDc4ODc5ZDUzYjZkOTYwZWYxN2ZiNGYyMmEzODZkNTJlY2UwMGE0Njg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commit/9a446c57f10de3bff219cf6abe76c59833d5926c","sha":"9a446c57f10de3bff219cf6abe76c59833d5926c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commits/9a446c57f10de3bff219cf6abe76c59833d5926c"}],"sha":"78879d53b6d960ef17fb4f22a386d52ece00a468","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commits/78879d53b6d960ef17fb4f22a386d52ece00a468"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commits/9a446c57f10de3bff219cf6abe76c59833d5926c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-09T01:00:39Z","email":"mcroker@gmail.com","name":"Martin Croker"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-09T01:00:39Z","email":"mcroker@gmail.com","name":"Martin Croker"},"message":"Add life-events-mfe''s multi-journey generalization to the PoC writeup\n\nNow that the rename/generalization (mfe-pot-employment-life-events-mfe ->\nmfe-pot-life-events-mfe, one journey -> a schema-driven kit authoring\nthree) is committed in both this repo and the sibling, fold it into the\nwriteup: repo table, a new design decision on the schema''s escape hatch,\na \"what was proven\" entry (qualified to what CI actually checked, not a\nmanual browser pass), and a new 08-09 timeline row.","tree":{"sha":"fa9bcb9fbeb9fea1e87144a8e9b7a676e2a04e3a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/git/trees/fa9bcb9fbeb9fea1e87144a8e9b7a676e2a04e3a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/git/commits/9a446c57f10de3bff219cf6abe76c59833d5926c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commit/9a446c57f10de3bff219cf6abe76c59833d5926c","node_id":"C_kwDOTqlj_toAKDlhNDQ2YzU3ZjEwZGUzYmZmMjE5Y2Y2YWJlNzZjNTk4MzNkNTkyNmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commit/41fc4ecbfaefbca372977cc98ff0222f69c7a0f6","sha":"41fc4ecbfaefbca372977cc98ff0222f69c7a0f6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commits/41fc4ecbfaefbca372977cc98ff0222f69c7a0f6"}],"sha":"9a446c57f10de3bff219cf6abe76c59833d5926c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commits/9a446c57f10de3bff219cf6abe76c59833d5926c"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tn4consulting/mfe-pot/commits/41fc4ecbfaefbca372977cc98ff0222f69c7a0f6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-09T00:58:09Z","email":"mcroker@gmail.com","name":"Martin Croker"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-09T00:58:09Z","email":"mcroker@gmail.com","name":"Martin Croker"},"message":"Rename mfe-pot-employment-life-events-mfe to mfe-pot-life-events-mfe\n\nRepo map, README clone/deploy instructions, TODO.md backlog, the VSCode\nmulti-root workspace, and both deploy-local.sh/deploy-eks.sh updated to\nmatch -- the sibling repo (GitHub remote included) was renamed as part of\ngeneralizing it from a single hardcoded \"you lost your job\" journey into\na family of life events (job loss, birth, disability today; death/\ncaregiving to follow) sharing one federated remote, fronted by a new\n/life-events hub page in mfe-pot-msca-shell. Dated docs/plans/ entries are\nleft referencing the old name, as historical record of when they were\nwritten.","tr