anizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alina9k/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alina9k/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alina9k/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alina9k/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alina9k/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alina9k","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kosumaster/DataMentor/commit/5be0f85862afcce0deda349c08683cc2dac807b2","node_id":"C_kwDOTrP1ydoAKDViZTBmODU4NjJhZmNjZTBkZWRhMzQ5YzA4NjgzY2MyZGFjODA3YjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kosumaster/DataMentor/commit/7d37120551fa23d381806ea0ca8a778076357fa4","sha":"7d37120551fa23d381806ea0ca8a778076357fa4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kosumaster/DataMentor/commits/7d37120551fa23d381806ea0ca8a778076357fa4"}],"sha":"5be0f85862afcce0deda349c08683cc2dac807b2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kosumaster/DataMentor/commits/5be0f85862afcce0deda349c08683cc2dac807b2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1560381?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tjementum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tjementum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tjementum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tjementum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tjementum","id":1560381,"login":"tjementum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1NjAzODE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tjementum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tjementum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tjementum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tjementum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tjementum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tjementum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kosumaster/DataMentor/commits/7d37120551fa23d381806ea0ca8a778076357fa4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-23T09:28:59Z","email":"tje@platformplatform.net","name":"Thomas Jespersen"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-02T10:09:49Z","email":"alina@unikk.me","name":"Alina Kazmirchuk"},"message":"PlatformPlatform PR 868 - Rebuild agentic workflow on Claude Code Agent Teams\n\n### Summary & Motivation\n\nIntroduces a multi-agent autonomous development workflow where\nspecialized AI agents collaborate to deliver complete features, from\nrequirements to production-ready code, while enforcing production\nquality standards. Built on [Claude Code Agent\nTeams](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/agent-teams), agents work like a\nreal engineering team inside the tools the user already uses. Features\nand tasks live in the user''s existing product management system (Linear,\nAzure DevOps, Jira, or markdown files on disk), not in a bespoke AI-only\ntracker. The full audit trail lives alongside the rest of the user''s\nwork.\n\n- **How the workflow runs**: the user starts the team lead with `pp\nclaude-agent team-lead`, points it at a feature or asks it to interview\nthem for one via `/create-prd`, and the team lead spawns the rest of the\nteam. From there, engineers move tasks from planned to active when they\nstart, reviewers move active to review when reviewing, and the Guardian\nmoves review to completed on a successful commit. The user watches\nprogress, comments on tasks, reprioritizes, adds bugs mid-flight, or\nrestarts tasks the agents got wrong, exactly like with a human team\n\n- **Agent roles**: the team lead coordinates the whole team and never\nwrites code. Persistent agents stay alive for the entire feature: the\n**Guardian** owns every git commit, Aspire restart, and final validation\nwith zero tolerance for failures; the **architect** tracks how the\nimplementation evolves across task sets and updates upcoming tasks when\nthings change; the **regression-tester** continuously validates the UI\nvia Claude in Chrome; the **researcher** investigates APIs and libraries\non demand. Fresh **backend**, **frontend**, and **qa** engineers plus\ntheir dedicated reviewers are spawned per task set and shut down in a\nrolling window, so no single agent accumulates context bloat\n\n- **Parallel task sets**: backend, frontend, and E2E tracks run\nconcurrently inside each task set. Engineers implement in parallel.\nReviewers validate independently and send one approval message per track\nwith the full file list. Once every track is approved and staged, the\nGuardian runs the pre-commit pipeline (build, test, Aspire restart, then\nformat, lint, and the smoke suite in parallel) and commits the tracks in\ndependency order\n\n- **Agents that actually collaborate**: Claude Code Agent Teams alone\nare fragile because `SendMessage` behaves like an inbox -- agents finish\ntheir current task fully before reading the next message, so mid-flight\nnudges go unheard. This introduces a custom `SendInterruptSignal` MCP\ncommand that pairs with an ID-correlated follow-up `SendMessage` and is\nauto-delivered by a `PostToolUse` hook as a blocking error on the target\nagent''s next tool call. Engineers interrupt QA when contracts change,\nreviewers interrupt engineers with in-progress findings, and agents talk\nto each other directly instead of routing everything through the team\nlead\n\n- **Zero-tolerance code review**: reviewers write an independent plan\nbefore reading the engineer''s code (to avoid anchoring), then validate\nline-by-line against the repository''s rule files. They reject on any\ncompiler warning, static-analysis finding, browser console warning, or\ndeviation from an established pattern -- including findings in unrelated\nparts of the system (Boy Scout rule). A PreToolUse hook nudges any agent\nthat tries to dismiss an issue with \"pre-existing\", and a Stop hook\nrepeats the nudge when the phrase appears at end of turn\n\n- **Plan before acting**: the team lead and pair-programmer start every\ntask in plan mode. They investigate first, present what they intend to\ndo, and only begin work after the user approves. Small tasks get brief\nplans; large tasks get detailed ones\n\n- **Explicit status ownership and andon cord**: every task-status\ntransition has exactly one owner (engineer starts, reviewer reviews,\nGuardian completes). Each agent verifies the expected state before\nacting. If anything is off -- wrong status, uncommitted changes from a\nprevious task, unresolvable validation failure, warning signal -- the\nagent pulls the andon cord: stop work and escalate. The team lead treats\nescalations as highest priority\n\n- **Tool-agnostic product management**: a single\n`PRODUCT_MANAGEMENT_TOOL` value in `AGENTS.md` selects Linear, Azure\nDevOps, Jira, or Markdown. Tool-specific details (status names, API\nshapes, ID formats, MCP configuration) live in\n`.claude/reference/product-management/{tool}.md` and are resolved by\nagents at runtime. Swap tools without changing any agent definitions\n\n- **Ad-hoc mode**: for small tasks that do not warrant the full team,\n`pp claude-agent pair-programmer` launches a single hands-on\ncollaborator that can still spawn sub-agents when a task benefits from\nparallel work or review\n\n- **Supporting changes**: `pp run` split into `pp run`, `pp restart`,\nand `pp stop` with matching `Run`/`Restart`/`Stop` MCP tools; detached\nmode is now the default and tails the AppHost startup log until ready.\n`pp claude-agent` sets `CLAUDE_CODE_EXPERIMENTAL_AGENT_TEAMS=1`\ncross-platform. The MCP server exposes separate\n`Build`/`Test`/`Format`/`Lint` tools with per-project log files, crash\ndetection, and a cross-process lock to prevent concurrent CLI builds\nfrom corrupting the cache. Bash hooks block `cd` and dangerous git\noperations. The README and `AGENTS.md` document the workflow end to end\n\n### Checklist\n\n- [x] I have added tests, or done manual regression tests\n- [x] I have updated the documentation, if necessary","tree":{"sha":"9d190a7c2325f8e23342836f7bcb19c7e7be079a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kosumaster/DataMentor/git/trees/9d190a7c2325f8e23342836f7bcb19c7e7be079a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kosumaster/DataMentor/git/commits/7d37120551fa23d381806ea0ca8a778076357fa4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/204223779?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alina9k/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alina9k/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alina9k/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alina9k/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alina9k","id":204223779,"login":"alina9k","node_id":"U_kgDODCw1Iw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alina9k/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alina9k/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alina9k/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alina9k/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alina9k/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alina9k","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kosumaster/DataMentor/commit/7d37120551fa23d381806ea0ca8a778076357fa4","node_id":"C_kwDOTrP1ydoAKDdkMzcxMjA1NTFmYTIzZDM4MTgwNmVhMGNhOGE3NzgwNzYzNTdmYTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kosumaster/DataMentor/commit/82e500db809a994a47c21328516492008eff7441","sha":"82e500db809a994a47c21328516492008eff7441","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kosumaster/DataMentor/commits/82e500db809a994a47c21328516492008eff7441"}],"sha":"7d37120551fa23d381806ea0ca8a778076357fa4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kosumaster