https://github.com/kosumaster/DataMentor/commit/71efae6dec1d5c1c4e399ba5f1b80ffe963bc63b","sha":"71efae6dec1d5c1c4e399ba5f1b80ffe963bc63b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kosumaster/DataMentor/commits/71efae6dec1d5c1c4e399ba5f1b80ffe963bc63b"}],"sha":"255c99eaa7a9e7d416fdb6d91ac8355fa2580099","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kosumaster/DataMentor/commits/255c99eaa7a9e7d416fdb6d91ac8355fa2580099"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/204223779?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alina9k/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alina9k/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alina9k/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alina9k/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alina9k","id":204223779,"login":"alina9k","node_id":"U_kgDODCw1Iw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alina9k/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alina9k/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alina9k/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alina9k/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alina9k/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alina9k","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kosumaster/DataMentor/commits/71efae6dec1d5c1c4e399ba5f1b80ffe963bc63b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-24T10:48:18Z","email":"alina@unikk.me","name":"Alina Kazmirchuk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-24T10:48:18Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Prevent duplicate questionnaire responses for the same participant (#344)\n\n### Summary & Motivation\n\nSaving and submitting a questionnaire response both follow a\ncheck-then-insert flow: the handler looks up an existing response for\nthe participant and, when none is found, creates a new one. The lookup\nand the insert run in separate transactions that only commit at the end\nof the request pipeline, so two requests racing through that window\n(most commonly a debounced autosave overlapping a submit) could each\npass the existence check and create a separate response row for the same\nparticipant and questionnaire.\n\n- Add a unique index on `(questionnaire_id, participant_id)` for\n`questionnaire_responses`, filtered on `deleted_at IS NULL`, so the\ndatabase rejects the second concurrent insert and a duplicate can never\nbe persisted regardless of request timing\n- Map the index in `QuestionnaireResponseConfiguration` so it is part of\nthe model used to build the test database schema\n- Add `ConcurrentQuestionnaireResponseTests` covering simultaneous save\nand submit for the same participant, asserting that exactly one response\nrow exists afterwards\n- Remove the temporary participant-endpoint model-binding diagnostic\nlogging from `ModelBindingExceptionHandlerMiddleware` that was added to\ninvestigate intermittent device upload failures\n\n### Checklist\n\n- [x] I have added tests, or done manual regression tests\n- [x] I have updated the documentation, if necessary","tree":{"sha":"be91ea16dc37cf43d7306239f941701da034e058","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kosumaster/DataMentor/git/trees/be91ea16dc37cf43d7306239f941701da034e058"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kosumaster/DataMentor/git/commits/71efae6dec1d5c1c4e399ba5f1b80ffe963bc63b","verification":{"payload":"tree be91ea16dc37cf43d7306239f941701da034e058\nparent 05335abe51bdfee8e5927fec51c819856d30f85c\nparent bd3accf3043c6032dd6e117b123c0a1f85ba05fe\nauthor Alina Kazmirchuk <alina@unikk.me> 1782298098 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782298098 +0300\n\nPrevent duplicate questionnaire responses for the same participant (#344)\n\n### Summary & Motivation\n\nSaving and submitting a questionnaire response both follow a\ncheck-then-insert flow: the handler looks up an existing response for\nthe participant and, when none is found, creates a new one. The lookup\nand the insert run in separate transactions that only commit at the end\nof the request pipeline, so two requests racing through that window\n(most commonly a debounced autosave overlapping a submit) could each\npass the existence check and create a separate response row for the same\nparticipant and questionnaire.\n\n- Add a unique index on `(questionnaire_id, participant_id)` for\n`questionnaire_responses`, filtered on `deleted_at IS NULL`, so the\ndatabase rejects the second concurrent insert and a duplicate can never\nbe persisted regardless of request timing\n- Map the index in `QuestionnaireResponseConfiguration` so it is part of\nthe model used to build the test database schema\n- Add `ConcurrentQuestionnaireResponseTests` covering simultaneous save\nand submit for the same participant, asserting that exactly one response\nrow exists afterwards\n- Remove the temporary participant-endpoint model-binding diagnostic\nlogging from `ModelBindingExceptionHandlerMiddleware` that was added to\ninvestigate intermittent device upload failures\n\n### Checklist\n\n- [x] I have added tests, or done manual regression tests\n- [x] I have updated the documentation, if necessary","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqO7XyCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAkPkQAE4IKgiH9LOGHFMLNilb77lV\n61k0aJTBxODlODy+GJwJ42IjWkQX0CFcSrjcitJ7UzDiQm+Q5CM2GQ3cBNlClZJy\nLYqjJOALRbwqXg5RfWJIyMdsz2Ucihi2xHDXKiv9ljTgEednSNvJhzMRUlJQ/l+4\nGwvNhpRaY2xA08jgXdIiuGBedtyb3OVIIdwa9rKjfhI7En+almkePP3NY/VMz+dE\nrM0IoAu0ZRuOIYRYt9DQyQbbSVH1EeTtElr8rSuAC4L1R3QSMvbAyG7FfbyHTMRP\np2urWT1itKMMtp1AcwVxZ2SDMx/8HHf4G5cRgWI/T5PPp4d4MV13XptqtssKao/S\nehkLswPVxxtxThsioUWfkSHCq7uTtJaPPbKZRjcQ7ngtIll6yBNQVufIRjELAUsv\n2K2ffMA/vqnUbP6BhwDlChzppNLblZ55lW060r+r02KntdadZekmdJU6Nfo2TyDS\n+6Lp66EZmekdbaRYPF/f5hvo5XVZTx8vufRnpaSkj13wUz4u12iPZdA0Nk364bz5\np86zRe5nQlGiqSdG5d4JRqdZf82b3pgHG0pWONKBytPkUbZTuMad9dYbzSPQ8p+i\nYtgstD8iDp8+ZzGtBkXzoocDQbg0SQW