Rodrigo Vieira"},"observedAt":"2026-10-09T00:01:39.351Z","repositoryId":1320942817,"sha":"fe45ab8316942b98bafe64be68bfcbf92e0078a1"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"rodvieira","providerType":"User"},"email":"rodrigodenizads@gmail.com","name":"Rodrigo Vieira"},"authoredDate":"2026-08-04T23:33:09Z","committedDate":"2026-08-04T23:33:09Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"rodvieira","providerType":"User"},"email":"rodrigodenizads@gmail.com","name":"Rodrigo Vieira"},"observedAt":"2026-10-09T00:01:39.351Z","repositoryId":1320942817,"sha":"6de3b532afceb25511e2f39cc61792145ff4d74f"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"rodvieira","providerType":"User"},"email":"rodrigodenizads@gmail.com","name":"Rodrigo Vieira"},"authoredDate":"2026-08-04T23:15:14Z","committedDate":"2026-08-04T23:15:14Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"rodvieira","providerType":"User"},"email":"rodrigodenizads@gmail.com","name":"Rodrigo Vieira"},"observedAt":"2026-10-09T00:01:39.351Z","repositoryId":1320942817,"sha":"47d1e2eb6eb08794bab4218b8dfc269715210356"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"rodvieira","providerType":"User"},"email":"rodrigodenizads@gmail.com","name":"Rodrigo Vieira"},"authoredDate":"2026-08-04T23:09:33Z","committedDate":"2026-08-04T23:09:33Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"rodvieira","providerType":"User"},"email":"rodrigodenizads@gmail.com","name":"Rodrigo Vieira"},"observedAt":"2026-10-09T00:01:39.351Z","repositoryId":1320942817,"sha":"a94de548b30d9c15461d2f75e08f17a2ee4d5550"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"rodvieira","providerType":"User"},"email":"rodrigodenizads@gmail.com","name":"Rodrigo Vieira"},"authoredDate":"2026-08-04T22:39:21Z","committedDate":"2026-08-04T22:39:21Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"rodvieira","providerType":"User"},"email":"rodrigodenizads@gmail.com","name":"Rodrigo Vieira"},"observedAt":"2026-10-09T00:01:39.351Z","repositoryId":1320942817,"sha":"d203b6c01cef0d0a43ab60750aceae4f67e8cede"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"rodvieira","providerType":"User"},"email":"rodrigodenizads@gmail.com","name":"Rodrigo Vieira"},"authoredDate":"2026-08-04T21:56:57Z","committedDate":"2026-08-04T21:56:57Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"rodvieira","providerType":"User"},"email":"rodrigodenizads@gmail.com","name":"Rodrigo Vieira"},"observedAt":"2026-10-09T00:01:39.351Z","repositoryId":1320942817,"sha":"c02cfe4d01632c3f981263c888e12fe473415924"}],"observedAt":"2026-10-09T00:01:39.351Z","raw":[{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35712292?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rodvieira","id":35712292,"login":"rodvieira","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1NzEyMjky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commits/d1958cc5d371b8fa858bbac43f5868518b0b99ec/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-23T19:49:32Z","email":"rodrigodenizads@gmail.com","name":"Rodrigo Vieira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-23T19:49:32Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Architecture review follow-ups: contract versioning, operational metadata, docs (#62)\n\n* docs(repo): describe the architecture that exists, and how to name an event\n\nThree gaps an external architecture review found, two of which were stale\nclaims left by the props refactor.\n\nCLAUDE.md still told anyone working here that the example remotes share \"a\ndesign system, an auth contract, and a typed event bus\" — the three things\nthat refactor removed, in the file that orients everyone. apps/dashboard''s\nREADME still said its stylesheet imports \"the design system''s tokens\" when it\nimports its own.\n\nThe bus had no governance at all. Payloads are `unknown` by design, so the\ncompiler is not part of that contract and naming is the only thing left\nholding it together — yet nothing said how to name a topic, who owns its\nshape, or that widening it is safe while renaming a field is not. That\nomission mattered more after the typed EventMap went away, not less. Also\nstates what the bus is not: not shared state, not request/response.\n\nAdds the architecture diagram the review asked for. It shows the two arrows\nthat matter — a URL read over the network, and the props handed back — which\nis the claim the whole design rests on and the hardest one to take on faith\nfrom prose. Rendered through mermaid and inspected rather than assumed.\n\n* feat(shell): let the registry say who owns a remote and how long to wait\n\nThree optional fields, for running more remotes than one person can hold in\ntheir head: `owner`, `criticality` and `timeoutMs`.\n\n`owner` and `criticality` change no runtime behaviour, on purpose. Every\nregion already fails in isolation, and making a critical remote retry harder\nwould hammer an origin that is already struggling. They change what a failure\ntells you: they ride along on every telemetry event, so \"payments failed to\nload, owner payments-team, critical\" needs no lookup table living somewhere\nelse. At two remotes that reads as decoration; at twenty remotes across\ntwelve teams it is the difference between a page and an outage.\n\n`timeoutMs` is the one with teeth. The host had a single 10s default, and the\nright budget is not a property of the host — a heavy reporting bundle on a\nslow internal network and a small widget on a CDN do not deserve the same\none. useRemote already accepted the option; nothing was passing it.\n\nAll three are validated like `version`: absent is fine, present-and-malformed\nfails at startup. A pipeline emitting `\"timeoutMs\": \"4000\"` has failed to\ncompute something, and coercing that quietly is how a remote ends up waiting\nforever. `NaN` is covered explicitly, because that is what a failed\ncomputation actually produces.\n\nTelemetry takes both labels as free-form strings rather than unions: who owns\nwhat, and how many severity levels there are, is the adopting organisation''s\nvocabulary and not an observability contract''s business.\n\nDeliberately no `retries`. Automatic retry without backoff turns one\nstruggling origin into a thundering herd, and a manual retry already sits in\nthe failure UI where a person decides. Backoff is a design, not a config key.\n\n* feat(shared-types): let a remote declare which props contract it implements\n\nNothing about this contract is checked at compile time. The props are\nstructural, and structural across two separately built applications means\nhope. That is fine while the shape only grows — a remote written a year ago\nkeeps working when the host adds a prop it ignores.\n\nIt stops being fine the day a prop is renamed or removed. A remote built\nagainst the old shape destructures `undefined` deep inside its own render,\nand what reaches an operator is a stack trace from someone else''s code with\nno mention of a contract at all.\n\nSo `HOST_CONTRACT_VERSION` names the shape, and the remote declares which one\nit implements by re-exporting it from the module it exposes. The declaration\nhas to come from the side that was actually built — a version recorded in the\nregistry would be the host asserting something about a remote it has never\nseen, which is a comment, not a guard. A remote in another repository\nhardcodes the number in its own copy of the contract, which is the point.\n\nThe check lives in the loader so an incompatible remote takes the\nload-failure path the host already contains and reports, naming both\nversions, rather than mounting and failing somewhere less legible.\n\nTwo deliberate choices. Declaring is optional, because every remote written\nbefore this says nothing and refusing those would break working deployments\nto guard against a hypothetical one. And the check is equality, not a range:\nthe failure being guarded against is a rename, where old and new are each\nvalid alone and only the pairing is wrong, so an older declaration is refused\nexactly like a newer one.\n\nGenerated remotes declare it in both modes. e2e still composes both example\nremotes through real federation, which is what proves the check does not\nreject the remotes it is meant to accept.","tree":{"sha":"d74af30e1afcfc44462e36e76918baedc7fd131f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/git/trees/d74af30e1afcfc44462e36e76918baedc7fd131f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/git/commits/d1958cc5d371b8fa858bbac43f5868518b0b99ec","verification":{"payload":"tree d74af30e1afcfc44462e36e76918baedc7fd131f\nparent 1a63e7ebc2fc92fbcef58c17ff106d21dd317f47\nauthor Rodrigo Vieira <rodrigodenizads@gmail.com> 1787514572 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787514572 -0300\n\nArchitecture review follow-ups: contract versioning, operational metadata, docs (#62)\n\n* docs(repo): describe the architecture that exists, and how to name an event\n\nThree gaps an external architecture review found, two of which were stale\nclaims left by the props refactor.\n\nCLAUDE.md still told anyone working here that the example remotes share \"a\ndesign system, an auth contract, and a typed event bus\" — the three things\nthat refactor removed, in the file that orients everyone. apps/dashboard''s\nREADME still said its stylesheet imports \"the design system''s tokens\" when it\nimports its own.\n\nThe bus had no governance at all. Payloads are `unknown` by design, so the\ncompiler is not part of that contract and naming is the only thing left\nholding it together — yet nothing said how to name a topic, who owns its\nshape, or that widening it is safe while renaming a field is not. That\nomission mattered more after the typed EventMap went away, not less. Also\nstates what the bus is not: not shared state, not request/response.\n\nAdds the architecture diagram the review asked for. It shows the two arrows\nthat matter — a URL read over the network, and the props handed back — which\nis the claim the whole design rests on and the hardest one to take on faith\nfrom prose. Rendered through mermaid and inspected rather than assumed.\n\n* feat(shell): let the registry say who owns a remote and how long to wait\n\nThree optional fields, for running more remotes than one person can hold in\ntheir head: `owner`, `criticality` and `timeoutMs`.\n\n`owner` and `criticality` change no runtime behaviour, on purpose. Every\nregion already fails in isolation, and making a critical remote retry harder\nwould hammer an origin that is already struggling. They change what a failure\ntells you: they ride along on every telemetry event, so \"payments failed to\nload, owner payments-team, critical\" needs no lookup table living somewhere\nelse. At two remotes that reads as decoration; at twenty remotes across\ntwelve teams it is the difference between a page and an outage.\n\n`timeoutMs` is the one with teeth. The host had a single 10s default, and the\nright budget is not a property of the host — a heavy reporting bundle on a\nslow internal network and a small widget on a CDN do not deserve the same\none. useRemote already accepted the option; nothing was passing it.\n\nAll three are validated like `version`: absent is fine, present-and-malformed\nfails at startup. A pipeline emitting `\"timeoutMs\": \"4000\"` has failed to\ncompute something, and coercing that quietly is how a remote ends up waiting\nforever. `NaN` is covered explicitly, because that is what a failed\ncomputation actually produces.\n\nTelemetry takes both labels as free-form strings rather than unions: who owns\nwhat, and how many severity levels there are, is the adopting organisation''s\nvocabulary and not an observability contract''s business.\n\nDeliberately no `retries`. Automatic retry without backoff turns one\nstruggling origin into a thundering herd, and a manual retry already sits in\nthe failure UI where a person decides. Backoff is a design, not a config key.\n\n* feat(shared-types): let a remote declare which props contract it implements\n\nNothing about this contract is checked at compile time. The props are\nstructural, and structural across two separately built applications means\nhope. That is fine while the shape only grows — a remote written a year ago\nkeeps working when the host adds a prop it ignores.\n\nIt stops being fine the day a prop is renamed or removed. A remote built\nagainst the old shape destructures `undefined` deep inside its own render,\nand what reaches an operator is a stack trace from someone else''s code with\nno mention of a contract at all.\n\nSo `HOST_CONTRACT_VERSION` names the shape, and the remote declares which one\nit implements by re-exporting it from the module it exposes. The declaration\nhas to come from the side that was actually built — a version recorded in the\nregistry would be the host asserting something about a remote it has never\nseen, which is a comment, not a guard. A remote in another repository\nhardcodes the number in its own copy of the contract, which is the point.\n\nThe check lives in the loader so an incompatible remote takes the\nload-failure path the host already contains and reports, naming both\nversions, rather than mounting and failing somewhere less legible.\n\nTwo deliberate choices. Declaring is optional, because every remote written\nbefore this says nothing and refusing those would break working deployments\nto guard against a hypothetical one. And the check is equality, not a range:\nthe failure being guarded against is a rename, where old and new are each\nvalid alone and only the pairing is wrong, so an older declaration is refused\nexactly like a newer one.\n\nGenerated remotes declare it in both modes. e2e still composes both example\nremotes through real federation, which is what proves the check does not\nreject the remotes it is meant to accept.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqi07MCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAE+8QAG/4QxPgexTruSDZbWqGZmNA\n+9tSUpMlOJ+nfqagQuFX1spkOd420qE9ev2aKTI6t4PFP208tJR2r02b+xPushis\nSl23+cdgibV6jKl5p6sJZT+CT2CAdoIgBYeidoWenZRRvCz35qgO6ZDoeklS+SpB\n4s0vbuW21L2srKwVBBsTlyqYtxUv5dLWBfhEdUiecWHoMD5bWAg02N22OIWDxJAW\nYXynibkJWM+KHzDUnC59r800/i+HNIAH8GJw35EX+HxE+GPgmZFFOkydzW6dzCaS\nC9IS36TYCRQHd2iW6khk8WoBE7zR5nHHNYd/YNDwnSo4jpPij8g2S/vql4d3wWLH\nvHbtzzRETsEapruer2NiFbkWQXYmxe++u8L5NDnEILOEElL3VmUpdl+R4DMm9UP2\nLpjEBTUOnfadTBIOgVXouXe3aKRZmkZ2fQx7BbhXd/RCLKiRDvZaRFrbZWj5nZLD\nwlCe0Era5g+XgwE6Vc1JPAZUNtxKQkttmnAZ8U3WI+i2le2leTRpLP3wFulAUq20\nB0UPMqU9EijfcLFKO1qSf04+QVvP/vffOEjKUfItW29vi09Fn8vWEedX7Ffgchpz\nLqWmJFp4znFb6LxAgkCfe8ftghVsO9yGnYRLDemGC2wP6zzWqmyZcqinpWTP6j0W\n/Y8gl1NA6u7libb/jpza\n=k8XP\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-23T19:49:32Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commit/d1958cc5d371b8fa858bbac43f5868518b0b99ec","node_id":"C_kwDOTrv84doAKGQxOTU4Y2M1ZDM3MWI4ZmE4NThiYmFjNDNmNTg2ODUxOGIwYjk5ZWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commit/1a63e7ebc2fc92fbcef58c17ff106d21dd317f47","sha":"1a63e7ebc2fc92fbcef58c17ff106d21dd317f47","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commits/1a63e7ebc2fc92fbcef58c17ff106d21dd317f47"}],"sha":"d1958cc5d371b8fa858bbac43f5868518b0b99ec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commits/d1958cc5d371b8fa858bbac43f5868518b0b99ec"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35712292?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rodvieira","id":35712292,"login":"rodvieira","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1NzEyMjky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commits/1a63e7ebc2fc92fbcef58c17ff106d21dd317f47/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T15:40:07Z","email":"rodrigodenizads@gmail.com","name":"Rodrigo Vieira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T15:40:07Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(repo): make the README demo reproducible, and portable after eject (#61)\n\nThe demo''s caption went stale because nobody could regenerate it. `pnpm\ndemo:record` turns the GIF into a build artifact of the real applications\ninstead of a screen capture whose provenance is lost.\n\nIt drives the actual apps through two same-origin iframes, so the shell''s\nBroadcastChannel relay genuinely carries the event between them. The\nrecording waits for the dashboard to reach 1,205 before writing anything —\nif the bus stops working the command fails rather than producing a GIF that\nmisrepresents it.\n\n`eject` takes the whole demo with it: the GIF films two applications the\nadopter no longer has, and the recorder has nothing left to drive. It also\nstrips `demo:record` and the three dependencies only the recorder needed,\nand removes the README''s image so nothing links to a deleted file. The prose\naround it still names the examples, which the review report picks up like\nany other mention.\n\nSeparately, chrome-isolation.spec.ts hardcoded /dashboard and /admin, so it\nwould have failed in every ejected repository. It now reads its routes from\nthe dev registry, and gained a narrow-viewport case: pinning the frame\noutside Tailwind''s layers had to keep the responsive behaviour, not replace\nit with a layout that is always a row.\n\nWorth noting what this exposed: `eject` used to remove every e2e spec, so\n`pnpm e2e` in an ejected repository passed having run nothing. It now runs\ntwo real specs there.\n\ngifenc has no published types, so scripts/gifenc.d.ts declares the surface\nthis script uses — an encoder change should be a compile error, not a\ncorrupt GIF.","tree":{"sha":"39bc4ece417d9810e6c80559c607d02c64cd0939","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/git/trees/39bc4ece417d9810e6c80559c607d02c64cd0939"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/git/commits/1a63e7ebc2fc92fbcef58c17ff106d21dd317f47","verification":{"payload":"tree 39bc4ece417d9810e6c80559c607d02c64cd0939\nparent 384e27edd86ddb37511b9c9beb5932afd6f7cf4e\nauthor Rodrigo Vieira <rodrigodenizads@gmail.com> 1787240407 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787240407 -0300\n\nchore(repo): make the README demo reproducible, and portable after eject (#61)\n\nThe demo''s caption went stale because nobody could regenerate it. `pnpm\ndemo:record` turns the GIF into a build artifact of the real applications\ninstead of a screen capture whose provenance is lost.\n\nIt drives the actual apps through two same-origin iframes, so the shell''s\nBroadcastChannel relay genuinely carries the event between them. The\nrecording waits for the dashboard to reach 1,205 before writing anything —\nif the bus stops working the command fails rather than producing a GIF that\nmisrepresents it.\n\n`eject` takes the whole demo with it: the GIF films two applications the\nadopter no longer has, and the recorder has nothing left to drive. It also\nstrips `demo:record` and the three dependencies only the recorder needed,\nand removes the README''s image so nothing links to a deleted file. The prose\naround it still names the examples, which the review report picks up like\nany other mention.\n\nSeparately, chrome-isolation.spec.ts hardcoded /dashboard and /admin, so it\nwould have failed in every ejected repository. It now reads its routes from\nthe dev registry, and gained a narrow-viewport case: pinning the frame\noutside Tailwind''s layers had to keep the responsive behaviour, not replace\nit with a layout that is always a row.\n\nWorth noting what this exposed: `eject` used to remove every e2e spec, so\n`pnpm e2e` in an ejected repository passed having run nothing. It now runs\ntwo real specs there.\n\ngifenc has no published types, so scripts/gifenc.d.ts declares the surface\nthis script uses — an encoder change should be a compile error, not a\ncorrupt GIF.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhx/XCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAPaEQAHLV/MCe+DDjxIOMufiPWftQ\n6i3o1uIHv0hDh4JNjdzP0VbCNTJdJj85QzwQD983f7yC6kO0x+tC8uNxMT30zKG8\niOZFbnQZA6WsFf/uGGs+f3acgfrGClslmTNh/38f2q2vbCyfg8HGKKNcoyg04sc9\nmmJfgU3kmsjQMtV2ybtZLVxvNFCZ7tsgYx8gryMcFmQQDFw+V1ED5sVrK0LOuTj9\nMyumkF23t7Eh9JwSAQTlFeuhYyojNmIWxOCIA6GwB2glsLxeyBTPn8qI3E0jKgv9\nJuqdyhfbCiPCNsZNrznqLy+jf+OxvXY4SC8aIj0biheqSgR8QS52H/dRB2a5yYDO\nD3sV76MSVNR56QFVSiW5qKzG53QLJrhXsIJzHiH5Qvy4EjV/MNXP8N+KayJUbPtv\nhj4izr8kuoiS8MtA+QWuQ0mm5PUCWjV01LaRRFX/wOP/DzzT/KC4SWt23n/gKW6w\nPCofxPgheEdyEzi0lJ3Rpo+nP3IqkHSw8IojDLVv5nseR0e7P5ZfU/YWTW8Bmyfa\nOokc15sA/W1zXy58HAh0LUgVDED3vp8kNI9M2FIbJw6iBla4Bs4W/JpY5Z6/y/Wt\nwMSmt9Wi6pLI6RoM1fzn0T+JAyeet3ejBOg4HRdUrFrHTGobk4EXZg7n2NY923im\nlltu9dewLSdl4BY8difB\n=CTtr\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-20T15:40:07Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commit/1a63e7ebc2fc92fbcef58c17ff106d21dd317f47","node_id":"C_kwDOTrv84doAKDFhNjNlN2ViYzJmYzkyZmJjZWY1OGMxN2ZmMTA2ZDIxZGQzMTdmNDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commit/384e27edd86ddb37511b9c9beb5932afd6f7cf4e","sha":"384e27edd86ddb37511b9c9beb5932afd6f7cf4e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commits/384e27edd86ddb37511b9c9beb5932afd6f7cf4e"}],"sha":"1a63e7ebc2fc92fbcef58c17ff106d21dd317f47","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commits/1a63e7ebc2fc92fbcef58c17ff106d21dd317f47"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35712292?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rodvieira","id":35712292,"login":"rodvieira","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1NzEyMjky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commits/384e27edd86ddb37511b9c9beb5932afd6f7cf4e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T18:29:34Z","email":"rodrigodenizads@gmail.com","name":"Rodrigo Vieira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T18:29:34Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs(repo): re-record the demo, whose caption described the old architecture (#60)\n\nThe GIF''s burned-in caption read \"typed event bus\". That bus no longer\nexists: the typed EventMap was removed when everything crossing the host\nboundary became a prop, and the bus is now owned by the shell, handed to\neach remote, and carries `unknown` payloads validated by the receiver.\n\nThe visuals were still accurate — the narrow panes stack the nav on purpose,\nwhich is the correct layout at that width, not the frame bug fixed in the\nprevious commit. Only the words were wrong, and they described the one thing\nthe demo exists to explain.\n\nRe-recorded against the real apps rather than edited. The new take also\nholds the dashboard pinned on its KPI for the whole clip, so the payoff is\non screen when the number moves, and ends on a frame where the admin table\nshows Ada Lovelace already switched to `editor` — the cause and the effect\nvisible at once.\n\nEncoded with a single global palette and unchanged pixels left transparent,\nwhich is why a longer, larger clip still lands at 108 KB.","tree":{"sha":"d6a248531f24bbc85990118bb3eae94bfc31bb43","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/git/trees/d6a248531f24bbc85990118bb3eae94bfc31bb43"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/git/commits/384e27edd86ddb37511b9c9beb5932afd6f7cf4e","verification":{"payload":"tree d6a248531f24bbc85990118bb3eae94bfc31bb43\nparent b58e46a5e67eb6fe4c0c49c30d06c36d6adc52f5\nauthor Rodrigo Vieira <rodrigodenizads@gmail.com> 1787164174 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787164174 -0300\n\ndocs(repo): re-record the demo, whose caption described the old architecture (#60)\n\nThe GIF''s burned-in caption read \"typed event bus\". That bus no longer\nexists: the typed EventMap was removed when everything crossing the host\nboundary became a prop, and the bus is now owned by the shell, handed to\neach remote, and carries `unknown` payloads validated by the receiver.\n\nThe visuals were still accurate — the narrow panes stack the nav on purpose,\nwhich is the correct layout at that width, not the frame bug fixed in the\nprevious commit. Only the words were wrong, and they described the one thing\nthe demo exists to explain.\n\nRe-recorded against the real apps rather than edited. The new take also\nholds the dashboard pinned on its KPI for the whole clip, so the payoff is\non screen when the number moves, and ends on a frame where the admin table\nshows Ada Lovelace already switched to `editor` — the cause and the effect\nvisible at once.\n\nEncoded with a single global palette and unchanged pixels left transparent,\nwhich is why a longer, larger clip still lands at 108 KB.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhfYOCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAFksQAKCmJsZbhm36vhwjvXpiyH9+\nyevW8exO1AMb/HGO8YEgort1QLBP2K7kITq00dKnvtwrerSaNwvuUk25ywE7ZL1Q\nVXXlzAhnHGZdw80v3wqKyRLo49wHEnSkr/w9N/t5/Fhhua9bh6M4ymHEVBLzgfRF\n2MVFaoZN7OFsH9/dJfLxpX6zTfLr0XjeQFzsbeTiNs+OpX2vl38yGXTkt2biwj79\nVavCOKVG48hj4KfUzeTop7cwO9SAYq0iMDt2shPJtnuCq+dJBwMn6CBctjBmfjlw\nCqFo7rBRopjlkse7A5GcAkbILjkP2HR1B/1W3lolSkQ48TSisBhu4aNDPwB2BxXq\nPcGiosYUVrfj07qD914C9nziCnBdhnDqfVG+Lv7t7VwEWVvl18TcCD0mupRxwwKo\nNvSSJI+G/XWbiLoJ3o7/qHMkS2u+U3OAD/asvUPTj8iDggPptpZ2/7U8LgXCIIWr\nPjl1d2ZgrHpRJHY0PMViNoHuIgbip3ze8to/5Psbfpd8D3AjF1lp6dxsf0ZImEBn\nndMjWZLGxP1verM/EF0jgG5Ts9wuAhsMhQ9/rISXa6EmDxWiuYlZelLAGPF/jrD4\nF0V9ptS/EV4RwfO6an3JBDCep1gnn0v6B5mVeLarfMW/Kf0Pi+4aDsa6VGlvd8+Y\naO6uc+32ZB9yPqm1ujQs\n=UsCL\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-19T18:29:35Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commit/384e27edd86ddb37511b9c9beb5932afd6f7cf4e","node_id":"C_kwDOTrv84doAKDM4NGUyN2VkZDg2ZGRiMzc1MTFiOWM5YmViNTkzMmFmZDZmN2NmNGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commit/b58e46a5e67eb6fe4c0c49c30d06c36d6adc52f5","sha":"b58e46a5e67eb6fe4c0c49c30d06c36d6adc52f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commits/b58e46a5e67eb6fe4c0c49c30d06c36d6adc52f5"}],"sha":"384e27edd86ddb37511b9c9beb5932afd6f7cf4e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commits/384e27edd86ddb37511b9c9beb5932afd6f7cf4e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35712292?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rodvieira","id":35712292,"login":"rodvieira","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1NzEyMjky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commits/b58e46a5e67eb6fe4c0c49c30d06c36d6adc52f5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T17:22:23Z","email":"rodrigodenizads@gmail.com","name":"Rodrigo Vieira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T17:22:23Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(shell): keep the host frame from losing the cascade to a remote (#59)\n\n* docs(repo): lead with the orchestrator, and drop a claim that is no longer true\n\nThe README still told adopters that a standalone generated remote consumes\n`packages/*` \"from whichever registry you publish your own scope to\". That\nstopped being true when the props contract landed: standalone output now\ndepends on nothing from here and installs from the public registry.\n\nAdds the section an adopter actually arrives looking for — how to point the\nshell at micro-frontends that already exist, in other repositories — with the\nregistry entry, the three things such a remote must do, and where\n`allowedOrigins` fits.\n\nAlso fixes two spots left stale by the refactor: `check:shared-deps` no longer\nguards `auth`/`event-bus`, and \"How the pieces fit\" described `packages/*` as\n\"contracts shared by all of them\", which is exactly the arrangement that was\nremoved.\n\n* fix(shell): keep the host frame from losing the cascade to a remote\n\nThe sidebar collapsed to a stacked layout the moment the shared UI package\nwas removed, on the live site, with nothing thrown and nothing logged.\n\nEvery app compiles its own Tailwind bundle and a remote''s stylesheet loads\nafter the host''s. Utilities are global single-class selectors, so the last\nstylesheet wins any tie — and a remote only emits the utilities its own\nsource uses. The host''s frame relied on `md:flex-row`, which no remote emits\nany more, while every remote still emits a plain `.flex-col`. The remote''s\nbase utility outranked the host''s responsive one.\n\nUntil the UI package was removed this resolved in the host''s favour by\naccident: every app scanned the same package source, so every bundle\nhappened to contain the host''s responsive utilities too.\n\nThe frame''s structural rules now live in `internal/chrome/frame.css` as\nplain CSS outside any `@layer`. Unlayered CSS outranks every layer and\nTailwind puts all of its output in layers, so the frame is immune to\nwhatever any remote ships. Appearance stays on utilities — a remote emitting\nthe same `border-b` declares the same thing.\n\n`e2e/chrome-isolation.spec.ts` asserts geometry rather than visibility,\nwhich is the only thing that catches this. It fails on the previous commit.","tree":{"sha":"17910cc9c08b8a98f99f5d438268208f3bc2c303","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/git/trees/17910cc9c08b8a98f99f5d438268208f3bc2c303"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/git/commits/b58e46a5e67eb6fe4c0c49c30d06c36d6adc52f5","verification":{"payload":"tree 17910cc9c08b8a98f99f5d438268208f3bc2c303\nparent 09a66642260ca14ed65d11592d565529ff5a97eb\nauthor Rodrigo Vieira <rodrigodenizads@gmail.com> 1787160143 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787160143 -0300\n\nfix(shell): keep the host frame from losing the cascade to a remote (#59)\n\n* docs(repo): lead with the orchestrator, and drop a claim that is no longer true\n\nThe README still told adopters that a standalone generated remote consumes\n`packages/*` \"from whichever registry you publish your own scope to\". That\nstopped being true when the props contract landed: standalone output now\ndepends on nothing from here and installs from the public registry.\n\nAdds the section an adopter actually arrives looking for — how to point the\nshell at micro-frontends that already exist, in other repositories — with the\nregistry entry, the three things such a remote must do, and where\n`allowedOrigins` fits.\n\nAlso fixes two spots left stale by the refactor: `check:shared-deps` no longer\nguards `auth`/`event-bus`, and \"How the pieces fit\" described `packages/*` as\n\"contracts shared by all of them\", which is exactly the arrangement that was\nremoved.\n\n* fix(shell): keep the host frame from losing the cascade to a remote\n\nThe sidebar collapsed to a stacked layout the moment the shared UI package\nwas removed, on the live site, with nothing thrown and nothing logged.\n\nEvery app compiles its own Tailwind bundle and a remote''s stylesheet loads\nafter the host''s. Utilities are global single-class selectors, so the last\nstylesheet wins any tie — and a remote only emits the utilities its own\nsource uses. The host''s frame relied on `md:flex-row`, which no remote emits\nany more, while every remote still emits a plain `.flex-col`. The remote''s\nbase utility outranked the host''s responsive one.\n\nUntil the UI package was removed this resolved in the host''s favour by\naccident: every app scanned the same package source, so every bundle\nhappened to contain the host''s responsive utilities too.\n\nThe frame''s structural rules now live in `internal/chrome/frame.css` as\nplain CSS outside any `@layer`. Unlayered CSS outranks every layer and\nTailwind puts all of its output in layers, so the frame is immune to\nwhatever any remote ships. Appearance stays on utilities — a remote emitting\nthe same `border-b` declares the same thing.\n\n`e2e/chrome-isolation.spec.ts` asserts geometry rather than visibility,\nwhich is the only thing that catches this. It fails on the previous commit.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqheZPCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA6VUQAEy1hSxCjhpp9L0h6QCbVvhc\n6D2jNcfb1Z11lfff3L1qMfMT0pWxXFSDSCsVwNg7u7eZepMBVw6iWPkL1I8W5sUq\nxUbzBnRIWFqBAT8xO3YY9MiWiVIKZADIavsxzVqy2aMbj+tEjEchYKLwClNLSUZQ\n9ouO5JPbGLNnUqLt9E/lcIQomDDvHBGajXd/ySi7ANLw+IjWsjVw9V5HP85j95c8\nuBV/vcBlG88Q+hcIeAVNNy8AuOaUfBrku5DagJpn4x5NSHU6IW3PyTVKG51CXN6U\nUDB1ic4EkTgQjrO7x08CBRvtwtsbmCUIlshWLy4WyOug+9TfnmQTVwdJNXK1DV9a\nzaQOtrm7UAcsas7rGHkKwsNOkYk+amCFGuhSs8tryv8ALcnMUcabm98VAJMot2n0\namj3M9hrRxO+7HlN86Qr/dH4g4NUPOnmJY/ljGio9+f4o1pp8j8KLlSrhr1QiiGu\nReXHjCAEHI+waBJ9Nu9IAE1Dy0Uey79NJjUEQy3bq6MDGTid+iE3h3pFfMPFf8yx\nHr0gi5ft4wsYqi6tk0Opo9y7wvQKz/2PK+oyu/Mvzlcbk0AZFZE0oqSMfb9cdfqm\ne0i4JdZ6Y5unq5X/tiVwqf/e+RJoeW/LvFA0eSByW87TrIkRsPajKLrp4jjhYhWR\nPHqoZD3h2vZv2vQ8Yioc\n=RSuk\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-19T17:22:23Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commit/b58e46a5e67eb6fe4c0c49c30d06c36d6adc52f5","node_id":"C_kwDOTrv84doAKGI1OGU0NmE1ZTY3ZWI2ZmU0YzBjNDljMzBkMDZjMzZkNmFkYzUyZjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commit/09a66642260ca14ed65d11592d565529ff5a97eb","sha":"09a66642260ca14ed65d11592d565529ff5a97eb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commits/09a66642260ca14ed65d11592d565529ff5a97eb"}],"sha":"b58e46a5e67eb6fe4c0c49c30d06c36d6adc52f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commits/b58e46a5e67eb6fe4c0c49c30d06c36d6adc52f5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35712292?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rodvieira","id":35712292,"login":"rodvieira","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1NzEyMjky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commits/09a66642260ca14ed65d11592d565529ff5a97eb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T02:25:14Z","email":"rodrigodenizads@gmail.com","name":"Rodrigo Vieira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T02:25:14Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(repo): make a remote need nothing from this project but props (#58)\n\nThe real deployment model for this boilerplate is an orchestrator: the\nmicro-frontends live in other repositories, are built by other teams, and\nare deployed to other URLs. The shell is given those URLs and composes\nthem.\n\nThe repository contradicted that. Three of the shared packages — `ui`,\n`auth`, `event-bus` — only worked for a remote that could *install* them,\nwhich needs a registry this project deliberately does not publish to. They\nwere therefore useless to exactly the audience they were written for, and\n`ui` doubly so: every large organisation already has a design system.\n\nEverything crossing the boundary is now a prop. `RemoteAppProps` carries\n`basePath`, `session`, and `bus`; `packages/shared-types` defines the whole\ncontract in about twenty lines, which a remote in another repository copies\nrather than installs — a type cannot cross a Module Federation boundary\nanyway, since host and remote are separate builds.\n\n- `packages/ui` -> `apps/shell/src/internal/chrome/`, plus a per-app copy of\n  what each example remote actually uses.\n- `packages/auth` -> `apps/shell/src/internal/session/`. Session is the\n  orchestrator''s job, not a distributed contract. `useAuth` is `useSession`.\n- `packages/event-bus` -> `apps/shell/src/internal/bus/`, keeping the\n  BroadcastChannel relay and its receiving-edge validation.\n- `apps/dashboard` and `apps/admin` import none of ours, which is the same\n  position a team in another repository is in. The cross-remote KPI still\n  moves across two tabs — e2e covers it.\n- The generator''s standalone mode now produces a project with zero\n  `@enterprise-mfe` dependencies: no `.npmrc`, no `GITHUB_TOKEN`, no \"install\n  fails until you publish\" caveat. `write-app.test.ts` guards that.\n\n`EventMap`''s compile-time topic union is the real cost, and it is the honest\nprice of remotes from other repos: no type survives independent builds.\nPayloads are validated where they are received instead.\n\ncheck:shared-deps shrinks to react, react-dom, react-router, telemetry and\ntailwind — not a loosened guard rail, just fewer things that can diverge.","tree":{"sha":"c10da4c147e525e4df6384fb73434fc07792a09c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/git/trees/c10da4c147e525e4df6384fb73434fc07792a09c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/git/commits/09a66642260ca14ed65d11592d565529ff5a97eb","verification":{"payload":"tree c10da4c147e525e4df6384fb73434fc07792a09c\nparent adc2544ff40c8756a7e5c5965a44fd570855d8e6\nauthor Rodrigo Vieira <rodrigodenizads@gmail.com> 1787106314 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787106314 -0300\n\nfeat(repo): make a remote need nothing from this project but props (#58)\n\nThe real deployment model for this boilerplate is an orchestrator: the\nmicro-frontends live in other repositories, are built by other teams, and\nare deployed to other URLs. The shell is given those URLs and composes\nthem.\n\nThe repository contradicted that. Three of the shared packages — `ui`,\n`auth`, `event-bus` — only worked for a remote that could *install* them,\nwhich needs a registry this project deliberately does not publish to. They\nwere therefore useless to exactly the audience they were written for, and\n`ui` doubly so: every large organisation already has a design system.\n\nEverything crossing the boundary is now a prop. `RemoteAppProps` carries\n`basePath`, `session`, and `bus`; `packages/shared-types` defines the whole\ncontract in about twenty lines, which a remote in another repository copies\nrather than installs — a type cannot cross a Module Federation boundary\nanyway, since host and remote are separate builds.\n\n- `packages/ui` -> `apps/shell/src/internal/chrome/`, plus a per-app copy of\n  what each example remote actually uses.\n- `packages/auth` -> `apps/shell/src/internal/session/`. Session is the\n  orchestrator''s job, not a distributed contract. `useAuth` is `useSession`.\n- `packages/event-bus` -> `apps/shell/src/internal/bus/`, keeping the\n  BroadcastChannel relay and its receiving-edge validation.\n- `apps/dashboard` and `apps/admin` import none of ours, which is the same\n  position a team in another repository is in. The cross-remote KPI still\n  moves across two tabs — e2e covers it.\n- The generator''s standalone mode now produces a project with zero\n  `@enterprise-mfe` dependencies: no `.npmrc`, no `GITHUB_TOKEN`, no \"install\n  fails until you publish\" caveat. `write-app.test.ts` guards that.\n\n`EventMap`''s compile-time topic union is the real cost, and it is the honest\nprice of remotes from other repos: no type survives independent builds.\nPayloads are validated where they are received instead.\n\ncheck:shared-deps shrinks to react, react-dom, react-router, telemetry and\ntailwind — not a loosened guard rail, just fewer things that can diverge.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhRQKCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAqnwQAHVlPaPrNpEZJOaTcrICLoiV\ntyXjB4LkacdGh3A5fN3G8bf/5vJdSH/WScxaaJQ/YAiZFP7Sfm1nBn0l71gCc/AT\nkOguph1uTgfzG60zeyzciCK0xINc02zthO7Cp/slFPP8vw7yxcnPtg2Xa4uM5e63\nxw3cJF0VcP/LcpJri5mLjWYhA8xhTfzPT9AeYIAR9qAm56ftMjuVRWVmR/Qfb1GW\nRzjoOgZqLJ7BiwC8ajvNWkIq8TCw7jVncdkOF0xJKnlhyhOPHxYhGllbdfHw4GxH\nbzedFFjqWuX/vssazWGApZMtECNbBiZ4LW1H9QwTn4yteEUAccFB5Bl+GzqUMReM\necUFM4cBWweccAjznUc5A0x+yEGJFdLT5OyMXcgFE0hME9a8Ln028nmww//ccfar\nHA0Q2y4h6NbK/uGVFBfseAcQfh1EKsGBLuSTXj/FnzSeC7IevtaIc+Gtddd3xhYF\nn54oUgFbX0fMVgIwx8lKpdrVj1z0DidUBtU3ss5PI3e6YhdS27KDPJt9pGxSd7bU\ntZoWO3rJVykvvkjVZBvKwiyufkzq2zdzd3j3hg4zxFrtXep0MxYqAU/jrFlwaN1C\n3P2FbOqiW9VpjuanFDiX+Ovj8en6F5pMjotXVaFczpoe+mlfRv376Zq21QfFzsz6\nN0qzcJhmKbuHy/gCSlGg\n=Q14+\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-19T02:25:15Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commit/09a66642260ca14ed65d11592d565529ff5a97eb","node_id":"C_kwDOTrv84doAKDA5YTY2NjQyMjYwY2ExNGVkNjVkMTE1OTJkNTY1NTI5ZmY1YTk3ZWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commit/adc2544ff40c8756a7e5c5965a44fd570855d8e6","sha":"adc2544ff40c8756a7e5c5965a44fd570855d8e6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commits/adc2544ff40c8756a7e5c5965a44fd570855d8e6"}],"sha":"09a66642260ca14ed65d11592d565529ff5a97eb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commits/09a66642260ca14ed65d11592d565529ff5a97eb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35712292?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rodvieira","id":35712292,"login":"rodvieira","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1NzEyMjky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commits/adc2544ff40c8756a7e5c5965a44fd570855d8e6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T01:21:55Z","email":"rodrigodenizads@gmail.com","name":"Rodrigo Vieira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T01:21:55Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs(repo): show the shared packages used together, not one at a time (#57)\n\nThe packages section listed each one with a snippet of its own, which\nanswers \"what is this package''s API\" and not the question someone actually\nhas on a fresh clone: how these fit together in one feature.\n\nAdds a worked example — a billing panel that lists invoices, gates the\naction behind a permission, and announces a paid invoice — using\nshared-types, auth, ui and event-bus in a single component, with a table\nsaying what each one contributed.\n\nIt starts with the part that is least obvious: adding a topic to the bus.\nTopics are a closed set, so a new event is a type addition plus a\nvalidator, and the docs now show the compiler error you get for omitting\nthe validator, because that guarantee is the reason the shape is worth\nfollowing.\n\nAlso names the two packages a remote should *not* call — telemetry and\nfederation-utils are host-side — since \"there are six packages\" invites\nreaching for all six.\n\nThe example deliberately does not live in the repository: it would be a\nthird example to delete on eject. Instead it points at the four real files\nalready running the identical pattern.\n\nVerified rather than written from memory: the component and the EventMap\nchange were compiled against the real packages in a scratch branch\n(typecheck clean, 14/14), the missing-validator error was reproduced to\nconfirm the wording (TS2741), and every file path in the closing table was\nchecked to exist and to contain what it is claimed to contain.","tree":{"sha":"647dce900841bdd1bbd5f1e8b2a7f787705f7031","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/git/trees/647dce900841bdd1bbd5f1e8b2a7f787705f7031"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/git/commits/adc2544ff40c8756a7e5c5965a44fd570855d8e6","verification":{"payload":"tree 647dce900841bdd1bbd5f1e8b2a7f787705f7031\nparent 350edc6668bd65f59fabf60680c1d280c8f1ea7e\nauthor Rodrigo Vieira <rodrigodenizads@gmail.com> 1787102515 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787102515 -0300\n\ndocs(repo): show the shared packages used together, not one at a time (#57)\n\nThe packages section listed each one with a snippet of its own, which\nanswers \"what is this package''s API\" and not the question someone actually\nhas on a fresh clone: how these fit together in one feature.\n\nAdds a worked example — a billing panel that lists invoices, gates the\naction behind a permission, and announces a paid invoice — using\nshared-types, auth, ui and event-bus in a single component, with a table\nsaying what each one contributed.\n\nIt starts with the part that is least obvious: adding a topic to the bus.\nTopics are a closed set, so a new event is a type addition plus a\nvalidator, and the docs now show the compiler error you get for omitting\nthe validator, because that guarantee is the reason the shape is worth\nfollowing.\n\nAlso names the two packages a remote should *not* call — telemetry and\nfederation-utils are host-side — since \"there are six packages\" invites\nreaching for all six.\n\nThe example deliberately does not live in the repository: it would be a\nthird example to delete on eject. Instead it points at the four real files\nalready running the identical pattern.\n\nVerified rather than written from memory: the component and the EventMap\nchange were compiled against the real packages in a scratch branch\n(typecheck clean, 14/14), the missing-validator error was reproduced to\nconfirm the wording (TS2741), and every file path in the closing table was\nchecked to exist and to contain what it is claimed to contain.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhQUzCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAADO0QAGnnQTu0FqqBGZpSseRunrvf\nOthw2ArDFnAZPNqm4y/6vBnGYf8KESA/cRt/wpZLQ4pwczhixKoW2ZYDU0vodnci\nPTxtIODSNy7C8sMHcrFJ4JKQ6eE00FO7jOh/JAyAQ75Jk4EHLmo9D7wq51ChHTaK\nKY7VuVc+BL+uejOe3cPQdJY0aMcAApiMAjxpmEBjp5c4ZCTona3vYw5dFtL0KhTw\nk77cXLdoLlcO4rDlL6NMelRB5dGZwHQtRztmT2HqkEx3p5/uRtQa36HyYlseCzmQ\ns6Y4iSNztuFeZUNInefo3zDgRwn8TnmUMIk6XIzuK+OX4/lFCg57Kdv5bihrvVRN\nWK8CDhIIXIqVrwkm2Mswnqqh8qvrm0ambxccU4k02/IfRtFBkKCP164ryj5kY/Rb\n7CrAv0MrPRP+iuuCBfjaNpJJXrUSgT0Mmuozsa9iFM4vcTjq+Zy1mp8mDa73+0Nk\n2P6VhDYZm554CGbD97jcPxw0rNbSn0uDfsF5xCUb9zB2B5gXmWmaJPw6rbJb8+0c\nF2HYmMe2W35mfa5EBPCJ8f/lgoINzr/Xo7vePQSB5rHYm0TSEiP8H/Kl+pCX6l7z\nTFPQVQWAP8R3f2klbatLpHc4dhc5OD6s93E+Um6UJzzPcIdgsELii782nstpjATP\n33x6hZH96OP1LCy+E6L0\n=7kAb\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-19T01:21:55Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commit/adc2544ff40c8756a7e5c5965a44fd570855d8e6","node_id":"C_kwDOTrv84doAKGFkYzI1NDRmZjQwYzg3NTZhN2U1YzU5NjVhNDRmZDU3MDg1NWQ4ZTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commit/350edc6668bd65f59fabf60680c1d280c8f1ea7e","sha":"350edc6668bd65f59fabf60680c1d280c8f1ea7e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commits/350edc6668bd65f59fabf60680c1d280c8f1ea7e"}],"sha":"adc2544ff40c8756a7e5c5965a44fd570855d8e6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commits/adc2544ff40c8756a7e5c5965a44fd570855d8e6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35712292?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rodvieira","id":35712292,"login":"rodvieira","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1NzEyMjky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commits/350edc6668bd65f59fabf60680c1d280c8f1ea7e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T01:04:33Z","email":"rodrigodenizads@gmail.com","name":"Rodrigo Vieira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T01:04:33Z","email":"rodrigodenizads@gmail.com","name":"Rodrigo Vieira"},"message":"docs(repo): fix references and claims left stale by earlier cleanups\n\nAn audit for anything a reader cannot resolve turned up two kinds of rot,\nboth left behind by removing the decision log and the spec folder.\n\nDangling ADR citations in six places — two app READMEs, two tests, and a\nCI comment — pointing at documents this repository no longer has. The\nmatches inside scripts/eject/transforms are deliberately kept: that module\nstrips ADR citations for a living, so an ADR reference is its test data.\n\nWorse, a section of apps/dashboard/README.md still described live\ncross-remote KPI updates as something that did not exist yet, on the\ngrounds that neither apps/admin nor packages/event-bus had been built —\ntext written when the dashboard came first. Both have existed for a long\ntime, and that update is the project''s headline demo. The section now\ndescribes what the remote actually does, including that it works across\ntabs.\n\nRemoving citations mid-sentence also broke prose in four places, which is\nthe same trap the eject is written to avoid: \"the second micro-frontend\nremote / a paginated/sorted user table\" with no connector, and two\nsentences ending in a bare \"See\". Rewritten rather than patched around.","tree":{"sha":"86cb72c315095c75aa5d247a0a54be71279246b9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/git/trees/86cb72c315095c75aa5d247a0a54be71279246b9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/git/commits/350edc6668bd65f59fabf60680c1d280c8f1ea7e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35712292?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rodvieira","id":35712292,"login":"rodvieira","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1NzEyMjky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commit/350edc6668bd65f59fabf60680c1d280c8f1ea7e","node_id":"C_kwDOTrv84doAKDM1MGVkYzY2NjhiZDY1ZjU5ZmFiZjYwNjgwYzFkMjgwYzhmMWVhN2U","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commit/d6b755e5f9600a68a0f5215d06c7ad2ef369652d","sha":"d6b755e5f9600a68a0f5215d06c7ad2ef369652d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commits/d6b755e5f9600a68a0f5215d06c7ad2ef369652d"}],"sha":"350edc6668bd65f59fabf60680c1d280c8f1ea7e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commits/350edc6668bd65f59fabf60680c1d280c8f1ea7e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35712292?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rodvieira","id":35712292,"login":"rodvieira","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1NzEyMjky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commits/d6b755e5f9600a68a0f5215d06c7ad2ef369652d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T02:34:15Z","email":"rodrigodenizads@gmail.com","name":"Rodrigo Vieira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T02:34:15Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(shell): let a registry entry be same-origin, and use it in production (#56)\n\nAn absolute entry has to be kept in step with wherever the shell actually\ngot deployed. When the two drift the shell fetches from a domain that does\nnot resolve, and it reads as a broken remote rather than a wrong string —\nwhich is exactly how the truncated Vercel project name presented. Preview\ndeployments have the same shape permanently: every preview URL is one\nnobody wrote down, so an absolute entry sends it to production''s remotes.\n\nA root-relative entry cannot drift, because it has no origin of its own to\nbe wrong about. Same-origin is allowed without an allow-list entry on\npurpose: it is the origin already executing the shell''s own code, so\nrequiring it to be listed would be a check that cannot meaningfully fail,\nand the generated CSP already covers it as ''self''.\n\nremotes.production.json now uses relative entries with an empty\nallowedOrigins, which tightens the generated policy to `script-src ''self''`.\nDev keeps absolute localhost entries — that is a genuine cross-origin case\nand still goes through the full check.\n\nTwo things the implementation is careful about, both found while writing\nit rather than after:\n\n- Same-origin skips the secure-transport check, including in the absolute\n  form. The shell''s own code already arrived over that scheme; refusing its\n  remote for using it protects nothing, and without this an http\n  deployment would work with a relative entry but not with the absolute\n  form of the identical URL.\n- `new URL(entry, base)` is only used for protocol-relative entries.\n  Passing a base unconditionally makes it resolve arbitrary junk —\n  \"not a url\" becomes \"<origin>/not%20a%20url\" — silently turning a\n  malformed entry into an allowed same-origin one. An existing test caught\n  that regression.\n\n`//host/path` still names another origin while looking relative, so it is\njudged as the third-party URL it is. A relative entry must be\nroot-relative: a bare `remotes/…` resolves against whatever route the\nperson is on.\n\nVerified that Module Federation actually loads a relative manifest, in a\nbrowser against the real assembled site: both remotes compose, no errors.","tree":{"sha":"f315dd49cf45cc4e9ea88758bd821a273449d11c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/git/trees/f315dd49cf45cc4e9ea88758bd821a273449d11c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/git/commits/d6b755e5f9600a68a0f5215d06c7ad2ef369652d","verification":{"payload":"tree f315dd49cf45cc4e9ea88758bd821a273449d11c\nparent ff3b714b1ff07740b67a7f50fca0096770a4f6e2\nauthor Rodrigo Vieira <rodrigodenizads@gmail.com> 1787020455 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787020455 -0300\n\nfeat(shell): let a registry entry be same-origin, and use it in production (#56)\n\nAn absolute entry has to be kept in step with wherever the shell actually\ngot deployed. When the two drift the shell fetches from a domain that does\nnot resolve, and it reads as a broken remote rather than a wrong string —\nwhich is exactly how the truncated Vercel project name presented. Preview\ndeployments have the same shape permanently: every preview URL is one\nnobody wrote down, so an absolute entry sends it to production''s remotes.\n\nA root-relative entry cannot drift, because it has no origin of its own to\nbe wrong about. Same-origin is allowed without an allow-list entry on\npurpose: it is the origin already executing the shell''s own code, so\nrequiring it to be listed would be a check that cannot meaningfully fail,\nand the generated CSP already covers it as ''self''.\n\nremotes.production.json now uses relative entries with an empty\nallowedOrigins, which tightens the generated policy to `script-src ''self''`.\nDev keeps absolute localhost entries — that is a genuine cross-origin case\nand still goes through the full check.\n\nTwo things the implementation is careful about, both found while writing\nit rather than after:\n\n- Same-origin skips the secure-transport check, including in the absolute\n  form. The shell''s own code already arrived over that scheme; refusing its\n  remote for using it protects nothing, and without this an http\n  deployment would work with a relative entry but not with the absolute\n  form of the identical URL.\n- `new URL(entry, base)` is only used for protocol-relative entries.\n  Passing a base unconditionally makes it resolve arbitrary junk —\n  \"not a url\" becomes \"<origin>/not%20a%20url\" — silently turning a\n  malformed entry into an allowed same-origin one. An existing test caught\n  that regression.\n\n`//host/path` still names another origin while looking relative, so it is\njudged as the third-party URL it is. A relative entry must be\nroot-relative: a bare `remotes/…` resolves against whatever route the\nperson is on.\n\nVerified that Module Federation actually loads a relative manifest, in a\nbrowser against the real assembled site: both remotes compose, no errors.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqg8SnCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAABmIQAFkowXX9lkzPrGjmogJ5EHIn\nuoQpmgSdrLfZgdjxngqqPHcY1Vqi6blz3WTXaUX27XlAvURCCEimvDnxnuiMtMJS\nPQmfHY+PipELbgJj8vvlc5C2Fk/CUi7ESLubwiVxsKvrn77wHTl+eMml+U6/5DhC\n+pKijcJt24asTg5FCr01HREhYT/KR9WJeLRpRlGx5v0a1xedXMTwQql8lIeH1Ats\n8MFzzYgeRLZAPCrmtk6YzL+VDMdeKDviJbkHNELwdjPANrhR59/XXym05Q+kxaHA\nW1S1vPgSwAuoJ0LeZkNilXPDtOAzX9w0WLw+1Wm8xIPtzjS/cRWm6/1/QghARdsl\nlIBbMIgWP7x/LzHY4xRZpXQ0suXZJaq1bYMLFa+RcnjCxf9KDfFpkFHbqoITmchi\nvoeJwrDI+Di+Is0FIpwELS3r0xgUlhhhbGSLdVdm5KE+xCJ2GVA0cX/KL7JPa15c\n671NQhVP0FKQX1Al7fLtyn3X/hff5DpSJwbxkONtGyZK7uIMNEc7hTjtgtTMqVKS\nqWSwAqS6+F9AJZ98wF1Ah+5iU3y2rNCdvfCJ4O2l0IdXeIFeWXw6Lq9An6NT0Nz2\nCclbZAKkie7ujhweefOB2HBZo9NmayUk/bCav3sxU3RaBhfa7aWRFbZfk1TiSRcn\nBGC9IaeeS43lf1Tp4pjB\n=0L0L\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-18T02:34:16Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commit/d6b755e5f9600a68a0f5215d06c7ad2ef369652d","node_id":"C_kwDOTrv84doAKGQ2Yjc1NWU1Zjk2MDBhNjhhMGY1MjE1ZDA2YzdhZDJlZjM2OTY1MmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commit/ff3b714b1ff07740b67a7f50fca0096770a4f6e2","sha":"ff3b714b1ff07740b67a7f50fca0096770a4f6e2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commits/ff3b714b1ff07740b67a7f50fca0096770a4f6e2"}],"sha":"d6b755e5f9600a68a0f5215d06c7ad2ef369652d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commits/d6b755e5f9600a68a0f5215d06c7ad2ef369652d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35712292?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rodvieira","id":35712292,"login":"rodvieira","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1NzEyMjky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commits/ff3b714b1ff07740b67a7f50fca0096770a4f6e2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T02:24:02Z","email":"rodrigodenizads@gmail.com","name":"Rodrigo Vieira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T02:24:02Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(repo): eject removes `pnpm rename` along with itself (#55)\n\nFound by running a full eject after the recent changes: rename survived\nit. In an ejected repository there is no old scope left for it to find, so\nit is a documented command that silently does nothing — the same reason\neject deletes itself.\n\nVerified end to end: after ejecting, scripts/ holds only build-site,\ncheck-package-exports, check-shared-deps and lib, package.json lists\nneither command, and the result still passes lint, typecheck and its 179\ntests.","tree":{"sha":"ff9f449214ef5d878efdd93b2a62c90505bd4f56","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/git/trees/ff9f449214ef5d878efdd93b2a62c90505bd4f56"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/git/commits/ff3b714b1ff07740b67a7f50fca0096770a4f6e2","verification":{"payload":"tree ff9f449214ef5d878efdd93b2a62c90505bd4f56\nparent 6e1ea1514f05cf8b53aeaff23d72b86c2c10ec96\nauthor Rodrigo Vieira <rodrigodenizads@gmail.com> 1787019842 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787019842 -0300\n\nfix(repo): eject removes `pnpm rename` along with itself (#55)\n\nFound by running a full eject after the recent changes: rename survived\nit. In an ejected repository there is no old scope left for it to find, so\nit is a documented command that silently does nothing — the same reason\neject deletes itself.\n\nVerified end to end: after ejecting, scripts/ holds only build-site,\ncheck-package-exports, check-shared-deps and lib, package.json lists\nneither command, and the result still passes lint, typecheck and its 179\ntests.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqg8JCCRC