ps://github.com/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commit/6e1ea1514f05cf8b53aeaff23d72b86c2c10ec96","sha":"6e1ea1514f05cf8b53aeaff23d72b86c2c10ec96","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commits/6e1ea1514f05cf8b53aeaff23d72b86c2c10ec96"}],"sha":"ff3b714b1ff07740b67a7f50fca0096770a4f6e2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commits/ff3b714b1ff07740b67a7f50fca0096770a4f6e2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35712292?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rodvieira","id":35712292,"login":"rodvieira","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1NzEyMjky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commits/6e1ea1514f05cf8b53aeaff23d72b86c2c10ec96/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T02:06:19Z","email":"rodrigodenizads@gmail.com","name":"Rodrigo Vieira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T02:06:19Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(ui): make the app frame fill the viewport (#54)\n\nThe Layout''s root used `min-h-full` — `min-height: 100%` — but nothing in\nthis project sets a height on html, body, or #root. A percentage height\nresolves against an ancestor that has one, so with none it collapsed to\nthe content''s own height and the browser''s white page background showed\nunderneath everything shorter than the screen. Measured: on a 900px\nviewport the frame was as tall as its content and no taller.\n\nNow `min-h-dvh`, which needs no cooperation from any ancestor and also\ntracks mobile browser chrome as vh does not.\n\ntokens.css also paints html and body with the surface and text tokens.\nThe frame filling the viewport is not quite enough on its own: an\noverscroll bounce still exposes the page behind it, and a remote rendered\nstandalone gets the right background either way.\n\nVerified in a browser at 900px: the frame is exactly 900px on both a\nnearly-empty route and a full one, and body resolves to the surface token.","tree":{"sha":"887e50538680355ac9ac018e0e88c64c10e2d55a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/git/trees/887e50538680355ac9ac018e0e88c64c10e2d55a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/git/commits/6e1ea1514f05cf8b53aeaff23d72b86c2c10ec96","verification":{"payload":"tree 887e50538680355ac9ac018e0e88c64c10e2d55a\nparent 2a681e02bf77eb2b6bd32eac3bbc6d12312bfff1\nauthor Rodrigo Vieira <rodrigodenizads@gmail.com> 1787018779 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787018779 -0300\n\nfix(ui): make the app frame fill the viewport (#54)\n\nThe Layout''s root used `min-h-full` — `min-height: 100%` — but nothing in\nthis project sets a height on html, body, or #root. A percentage height\nresolves against an ancestor that has one, so with none it collapsed to\nthe content''s own height and the browser''s white page background showed\nunderneath everything shorter than the screen. Measured: on a 900px\nviewport the frame was as tall as its content and no taller.\n\nNow `min-h-dvh`, which needs no cooperation from any ancestor and also\ntracks mobile browser chrome as vh does not.\n\ntokens.css also paints html and body with the surface and text tokens.\nThe frame filling the viewport is not quite enough on its own: an\noverscroll bounce still exposes the page behind it, and a remote rendered\nstandalone gets the right background either way.\n\nVerified in a browser at 900px: the frame is exactly 900px on both a\nnearly-empty route and a full one, and body resolves to the surface token.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqg74bCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAenoQAAsPfYOM/CfLYBA2MGC+3Y+U\ntzL8OPUa+kMYshMV4mP7fO7a0JxY+deiWaitLOWJW9+ry4hI2YgSsruxWDBW9HPc\nAXfu4B4a4VYabhcSWj/xTvvp9W3baJBI15FQptuRnRb/un9zg/2bsjXMI6TKzUzH\n+kzIgjCanNg01J69OdF4pameVORl/ymMm7IVwcjHnd2UaAMw4Emea9QKuc4I2/wI\nX8Sx1+RvwC9wQwgAYvAuxpbeXb/1z8orpNFzKjQT0UvFDH3pEMKyRiDt5danQ21K\nr38vbTMN2TbohUix1rxQAHaH85dfeYKKERm7tMkTX0eC7DZU3ONHpfZmSjUKBWwb\nYyGmwEQbbRv2U9JILp8PUMNId/esrb22lhG6Qd27KDwiAVQpdZ/oLoSaI4xGvqEa\nvdnRnDNQCVZY7Xa2Nt4epqUvQtlQ6GQJrEEK5+prgg4G2ah0MY0AtHN+3DHZVX7I\nf2TA6KMkhj+jNhnYaJPPvFiALoHj7TEDpNxd1wyppoTLoxX1xQqk+6uWuRfHtfhb\nhrEHJAfuWDX5QSskMqS1cqbOymiM54ww1X4jQMTRW+C6u0vyElRHz6eNhhFEAeSB\nkRhg91y5YkMUJ/MivNvR8aXzW4qMgItGw4KedNz+IxgtCeV1OXVwyD6BLxqc1nAJ\nMnBFqbsPswLyd6r2Uh/w\n=McoZ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-18T02:06:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commit/6e1ea1514f05cf8b53aeaff23d72b86c2c10ec96","node_id":"C_kwDOTrv84doAKDZlMWVhMTUxNGYwNWNmOGI1M2FlYWZmMjNkNzJiODZjMmMxMGVjOTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commit/2a681e02bf77eb2b6bd32eac3bbc6d12312bfff1","sha":"2a681e02bf77eb2b6bd32eac3bbc6d12312bfff1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commits/2a681e02bf77eb2b6bd32eac3bbc6d12312bfff1"}],"sha":"6e1ea1514f05cf8b53aeaff23d72b86c2c10ec96","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commits/6e1ea1514f05cf8b53aeaff23d72b86c2c10ec96"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35712292?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rodvieira","id":35712292,"login":"rodvieira","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1NzEyMjky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commits/2a681e02bf77eb2b6bd32eac3bbc6d12312bfff1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T01:56:15Z","email":"rodrigodenizads@gmail.com","name":"Rodrigo Vieira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T01:56:15Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(shell): point the production registry at the real Vercel origin (#53)\n\nVercel truncated the project name to `enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplat`\n— one character short of the repository name the registry was written\nagainst. So the shell served from `...boilerplat.vercel.app` was fetching\nits remotes from `...boilerplate.vercel.app`, a domain that does not\nresolve.\n\nWorth being precise about the failure: origin-guard did not refuse\nanything. The registry was internally consistent — the origin it listed\nmatched the entries it declared — so the guard passed and the fetch failed\nwith `TypeError: Failed to fetch`. The CSP would have blocked it too, for\nthe same reason: it is derived from the same allowedOrigins list.\n\nThe telemetry added earlier reported it cleanly on its first real\nincident: `[telemetry] dashboard (/dashboard) failed to load after 110ms`.\n\nOne string in remotes.production.json, plus the docs that quote the URL.\nThe CSP follows automatically because the build reads it from that file.","tree":{"sha":"1c4d4ceea45ac370bf51384277b87ee2f7c1fad6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/git/trees/1c4d4ceea45ac370bf51384277b87ee2f7c1fad6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/git/commits/2a681e02bf77eb2b6bd32eac3bbc6d12312bfff1","verification":{"payload":"tree 1c4d4ceea45ac370bf51384277b87ee2f7c1fad6\nparent 3bdda6e0659f79ec505803a0570648356bda3888\nauthor Rodrigo Vieira <rodrigodenizads@gmail.com> 1787018175 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787018175 -0300\n\nfix(shell): point the production registry at the real Vercel origin (#53)\n\nVercel truncated the project name to `enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplat`\n— one character short of the repository name the registry was written\nagainst. So the shell served from `...boilerplat.vercel.app` was fetching\nits remotes from `...boilerplate.vercel.app`, a domain that does not\nresolve.\n\nWorth being precise about the failure: origin-guard did not refuse\nanything. The registry was internally consistent — the origin it listed\nmatched the entries it declared — so the guard passed and the fetch failed\nwith `TypeError: Failed to fetch`. The CSP would have blocked it too, for\nthe same reason: it is derived from the same allowedOrigins list.\n\nThe telemetry added earlier reported it cleanly on its first real\nincident: `[telemetry] dashboard (/dashboard) failed to load after 110ms`.\n\nOne string in remotes.production.json, plus the docs that quote the URL.\nThe CSP follows automatically because the build reads it from that file.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqg7u/CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA6pcQAKhjWp1v3+25RN4qm8SqCf5y\nLpR033PnOujNpytSzGduXs8y7XS5ap3mcGsCz8wEv9bGi7TZ9+Y7EoDo69hajon9\nlIjQ+lMSQEN5j4ay40FaKgMiH+XVX66IW1qFbtlNmJ7hmVYYpDo8Sn7cgvs0jD1I\nFa5scSnCm4YSqyRaU0plWhLxPioDMMy2BluwFP+8mrkpg+Z+2b5goQ+79bIuH3Zc\npWpDdtFCNSsL7pXC3Y0O/emhrQL2LKeyrrmLcUQce6GL+ce5I9v1CiQHQINIRCcu\nndyc0wmjBr77dE+XLnFAr2OZqEvhnOpywC8lRt1T5jCDqt/Ewoif0ZOdVryICSKH\n382zOrQsb9NcKfUi8v4+eFrTWe1pnTMvmoR78mRgpTqBQ+C9C69PpKxMLh3YyHWP\nclAaQSJugHUmQVoGN4fm11pLKSzw0INexPEaqII1H44Gsz2hjw1jCQnw0QbtYB1t\nNVBEkPdguy/hoKzfXQF9r03/BnnXF6RP8E81Vbh9Cvx7GzOW2U9I5yZRu2ldZQit\nQC61geZ7RCklVyTD594U2TB/IQMstm/63wqL2eBP1rkGBXgLEsQkU1hoDq2KnSbs\noaLBqUxcMwe83+k13r3zriVIaJEC/+UHvW/esvJn1jLoWxU4ebEsucecuzvEV7sg\nurxydmh5a1PVyYFS/LhW\n=58yg\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-18T01:56:16Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commit/2a681e02bf77eb2b6bd32eac3bbc6d12312bfff1","node_id":"C_kwDOTrv84doAKDJhNjgxZTAyYmY3N2ViMmI2YmQzMmVhYzNiYmM2ZDEyMzEyYmZmZjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commit/3bdda6e0659f79ec505803a0570648356bda3888","sha":"3bdda6e0659f79ec505803a0570648356bda3888","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commits/3bdda6e0659f79ec505803a0570648356bda3888"}],"sha":"2a681e02bf77eb2b6bd32eac3bbc6d12312bfff1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commits/2a681e02bf77eb2b6bd32eac3bbc6d12312bfff1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35712292?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rodvieira","id":35712292,"login":"rodvieira","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1NzEyMjky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commits/3bdda6e0659f79ec505803a0570648356bda3888/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T00:06:55Z","email":"rodrigodenizads@gmail.com","name":"Rodrigo Vieira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T00:06:55Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(repo): add `pnpm rename`, and document deploying to any cloud (#52)\n\nRENAME. Making a clone yours already existed, but only inside `pnpm eject`\n— which also deletes both example remotes, generates a replacement, and\nremoves itself. That is the wrong trade on day one: you want your own name\non it while you are still reading the examples.\n\n`pnpm rename --scope @acme --name acme-platform` does the renaming and\nnothing else. The project name is not cosmetic — it is the root package\nname, the shell''s <title>, and the text in the shell''s own header, so this\nboilerplate brands whatever you ship until it is replaced.\n\nThe file walker is now shared with the eject rather than copied, so a\ndirectory or extension one of them learns about cannot be silently missed\nby the other.\n\nRunning it against a real copy found a bug in this repo''s own tests: the\nrenameScope fixture used the literal @enterprise-mfe, so renaming rewrote\nthe test''s *input* and turned the assertion into renameScope(x, ''@acme'',\n''@acme''). A pure function''s test should not depend on the repository''s\nidentity — it uses a fake scope now.\n\nDEPLOYING. The guide covered one host. It now covers what actually differs\nbetween them, which is only two things: whether the host can rewrite\nunmatched paths to index.html, and where the remotes'' files live. Then the\nconcrete setup for Vercel, Netlify, Cloudflare Pages, S3+CloudFront, Azure\nStatic Web Apps, nginx, and GitHub Pages — the last with its HTTP 404\ncaveat stated rather than buried.\n\nAdds the section neither the old docs nor the deploy had: deploying each\nremote to its own origin, which is the point of the architecture and the\nfirst configuration that genuinely exercises origin-guard and the CSP.\nPlus a short \"when a deployed remote does not load\", ordered by how often\neach cause is the real one.\n\nAlso fixes README leftovers from the ADR removal: a sentence broken\nmid-clause by a stripped link, and a claim that standalone remotes consume\n`packages/*` as published dependencies, which stopped being true when\npublishing was removed.","tree":{"sha":"6a970b3486a4cde00307ccea57a130271d03003b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/git/trees/6a970b3486a4cde00307ccea57a130271d03003b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/git/commits/3bdda6e0659f79ec505803a0570648356bda3888","verification":{"payload":"tree 6a970b3486a4cde00307ccea57a130271d03003b\nparent f81844a4049661d06d07c52b3e4e8c1e0a406da1\nauthor Rodrigo Vieira <rodrigodenizads@gmail.com> 1787011615 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787011615 -0300\n\nfeat(repo): add `pnpm rename`, and document deploying to any cloud (#52)\n\nRENAME. Making a clone yours already existed, but only inside `pnpm eject`\n— which also deletes both example remotes, generates a replacement, and\nremoves itself. That is the wrong trade on day one: you want your own name\non it while you are still reading the examples.\n\n`pnpm rename --scope @acme --name acme-platform` does the renaming and\nnothing else. The project name is not cosmetic — it is the root package\nname, the shell''s <title>, and the text in the shell''s own header, so this\nboilerplate brands whatever you ship until it is replaced.\n\nThe file walker is now shared with the eject rather than copied, so a\ndirectory or extension one of them learns about cannot be silently missed\nby the other.\n\nRunning it against a real copy found a bug in this repo''s own tests: the\nrenameScope fixture used the literal @enterprise-mfe, so renaming rewrote\nthe test''s *input* and turned the assertion into renameScope(x, ''@acme'',\n''@acme''). A pure function''s test should not depend on the repository''s\nidentity — it uses a fake scope now.\n\nDEPLOYING. The guide covered one host. It now covers what actually differs\nbetween them, which is only two things: whether the host can rewrite\nunmatched paths to index.html, and where the remotes'' files live. Then the\nconcrete setup for Vercel, Netlify, Cloudflare Pages, S3+CloudFront, Azure\nStatic Web Apps, nginx, and GitHub Pages — the last with its HTTP 404\ncaveat stated rather than buried.\n\nAdds the section neither the old docs nor the deploy had: deploying each\nremote to its own origin, which is the point of the architecture and the\nfirst configuration that genuinely exercises origin-guard and the CSP.\nPlus a short \"when a deployed remote does not load\", ordered by how often\neach cause is the real one.\n\nAlso fixes README leftovers from the ADR removal: a sentence broken\nmid-clause by a stripped link, and a claim that standalone remotes consume\n`packages/*` as published dependencies, which stopped being true when\npublishing was removed.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqg6IfCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAANGAQAD7P0m+0U/3EM++QQXrFQmq2\nqt9DEI2vMXI8tBBwBloeij5CX/lYNGlYnzLymKAvsDNqhZDh3K6n1rKGInzp8ZQu\nM++QXBJ/S4Ry3w+UCFGU9l7IbnrhkyBPTgKnXuOl6YU/q3+huTPx6V/P9lIjGObr\nvHsijATA6G7aocdmvbXk1dRhM5AJjRumUXzACpiOpD2