microfrontend-boilerplate/commits/f81844a4049661d06d07c52b3e4e8c1e0a406da1"}],"sha":"3bdda6e0659f79ec505803a0570648356bda3888","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commits/3bdda6e0659f79ec505803a0570648356bda3888"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35712292?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rodvieira","id":35712292,"login":"rodvieira","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1NzEyMjky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commits/f81844a4049661d06d07c52b3e4e8c1e0a406da1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-17T23:39:49Z","email":"rodrigodenizads@gmail.com","name":"Rodrigo Vieira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-17T23:39:49Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs(repo): one usage guide, and make the shared packages cover their own demo (#51)\n\nThree things, all pointed at the same person: someone who cloned this and\nwants to use it.\n\nDOCUMENTATION. The repo carried its own construction history — 26 ADRs, a\nspec folder per sprint, a 52KB blueprint, a constitution, and seven\ntopic-specific guides. None of that answers \"how do I use this\", and all\nof it is noise for an adopter. It is replaced by one docs/USAGE.md:\ncommands, a step-by-step from clone to your own platform, what each shared\npackage exports and how, adding a remote, deploying, and connecting real\nauth or telemetry.\n\nRemoving the decision log dangled 122 references across docs, source, and\ntemplates. Most were stripped with the eject''s own tested transform; the\nrest were rewritten by hand, including several README links that pointed\ninto the deleted specs/ tree and would have 404''d.\n\nPACKAGES. The design system did not cover its own demo. The admin remote\nhand-rolled three <select> elements with copy-pasted Tailwind, each\nmissing the focus ring and the error/hint wiring Input has — an\naccessibility regression the design system existed to prevent. There is\nnow a Select with Input''s exact contract, and the three copies are gone.\nThree raw <button> elements in shell and admin now use Button too.\n\nPUBLISHING. Removed the changesets setup and the publish workflow: this\nproject does not publish, and infrastructure for something nobody runs is\njust a thing that rots. The packaging itself stays correct and verified\n(tsup, publishConfig.exports, check:package-exports) so an adopter can\npublish their own scope on day one. The generator now says plainly that a\nstandalone project cannot install until you do.\n\nAlso closes #3: turbo.json declared a `test` task no package implements,\nso `turbo test` would have found zero tasks and exited 0 having run\nnothing. Removed, and CLAUDE.md now records why `pnpm test` is vitest\ndirectly.\n\nRemoving docs/architecture.md would have broken the generator, which\nappended to it on every run. That action is gone — with a single usage\nguide, a generator writing prose into it degrades the one doc that\nmatters.","tree":{"sha":"1a2987f56967eba09e551ec143f80a4c30eb6d93","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/git/trees/1a2987f56967eba09e551ec143f80a4c30eb6d93"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/git/commits/f81844a4049661d06d07c52b3e4e8c1e0a406da1","verification":{"payload":"tree 1a2987f56967eba09e551ec143f80a4c30eb6d93\nparent 4a9db63c71a2e5f167c04a7b837ad70702287e76\nauthor Rodrigo Vieira <rodrigodenizads@gmail.com> 1787009989 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787009989 -0300\n\ndocs(repo): one usage guide, and make the shared packages cover their own demo (#51)\n\nThree things, all pointed at the same person: someone who cloned this and\nwants to use it.\n\nDOCUMENTATION. The repo carried its own construction history — 26 ADRs, a\nspec folder per sprint, a 52KB blueprint, a constitution, and seven\ntopic-specific guides. None of that answers \"how do I use this\", and all\nof it is noise for an adopter. It is replaced by one docs/USAGE.md:\ncommands, a step-by-step from clone to your own platform, what each shared\npackage exports and how, adding a remote, deploying, and connecting real\nauth or telemetry.\n\nRemoving the decision log dangled 122 references across docs, source, and\ntemplates. Most were stripped with the eject''s own tested transform; the\nrest were rewritten by hand, including several README links that pointed\ninto the deleted specs/ tree and would have 404''d.\n\nPACKAGES. The design system did not cover its own demo. The admin remote\nhand-rolled three <select> elements with copy-pasted Tailwind, each\nmissing the focus ring and the error/hint wiring Input has — an\naccessibility regression the design system existed to prevent. There is\nnow a Select with Input''s exact contract, and the three copies are gone.\nThree raw <button> elements in shell and admin now use Button too.\n\nPUBLISHING. Removed the changesets setup and the publish workflow: this\nproject does not publish, and infrastructure for something nobody runs is\njust a thing that rots. The packaging itself stays correct and verified\n(tsup, publishConfig.exports, check:package-exports) so an adopter can\npublish their own scope on day one. The generator now says plainly that a\nstandalone project cannot install until you do.\n\nAlso closes #3: turbo.json declared a `test` task no package implements,\nso `turbo test` would have found zero tasks and exited 0 having run\nnothing. Removed, and CLAUDE.md now records why `pnpm test` is vitest\ndirectly.\n\nRemoving docs/architecture.md would have broken the generator, which\nappended to it on every run. That action is gone — with a single usage\nguide, a generator writing prose into it degrades the one doc that\nmatters.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqg5vFCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAG5wQAI1I2cfqHTZd7i4OTGDCvTMA\nIezD65lbXFdqYHpoyhNAgqhmOmiW5fBqY2+iGQJp/EKGpXXbzmUV56RqIV1ij+ux\nAN+k95+IKT9dhjFP9LKKHIUCECu2aQGy7g0MtSj1Ho0mbg+lifAPwoUjl5sSykNF\n4Q5w61vtiw1XmfSLb5vv8qR2ji78d8OEIqEpLAaZZrN2hhu2gRxxnl+hBqndpQoq\n0BOZcBEkspOCAoJEpI1VO1a8gEmradRyQQC6DwZlY5LL6i4MtE2YeFQOUGYMVEIk\nJFZUs8k+4wyBSzXk4GspBj1CgIUhQjqqs+yHUA8LqRbSPJcP8/iwWPJyFQ0O7OeG\nlB2KIkr3Orro2fJEs0qPE8pe27luK2uKzmI4Yn3JAk1WCsL+ULRzyj2v1e50C3Y1\nK1+EK5G4mmPTydjRCdOcBQ6IFnfLnnWcfEcktMJyejbpvqRAvdyKGF4iKehJHJQk\nptEyi4RcSxD1NlIflMIOhzbN0/IODRqEwdIf+Ikjg1MEowJ2WA9Hsw8tAHrJxuU3\nW72jm5Ab4xfT1fnauQmHwNFUSAKQGuPdSvhYOs+qqKiSsnYJAPT4qfsuFmh2GePo\ndTJeYe6LbJMcJkckREVHuIdRpx8dsli+PmLECqDBmc5tt5znbTeWJTM/YYcghJDn\ngy+N2LlirqWIzT3cweFR\n=SpzL\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-17T23:39:49Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commit/f81844a4049661d06d07c52b3e4e8c1e0a406da1","node_id":"C_kwDOTrv84doAKGY4MTg0NGE0MDQ5NjYxZDA2ZDA3YzUyYjNlNGU4YzFlMGE0MDZkYTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commit/4a9db63c71a2e5f167c04a7b837ad70702287e76","sha":"4a9db63c71a2e5f167c04a7b837ad70702287e76","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commits/4a9db63c71a2e5f167c04a7b837ad70702287e76"}],"sha":"f81844a4049661d06d07c52b3e4e8c1e0a406da1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commits/f81844a4049661d06d07c52b3e4e8c1e0a406da1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35712292?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rodvieira","id":35712292,"login":"rodvieira","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1NzEyMjky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commits/4a9db63c71a2e5f167c04a7b837ad70702287e76/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-17T23:08:54Z","email":"rodrigodenizads@gmail.com","name":"Rodrigo Vieira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-17T23:08:54Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(repo): move the reference deploy to Vercel, publish to npm (ADR-0026) (#50)\n\nA browser check of production found what curl smoke tests had missed:\n/dashboard and /admin returned HTTP 404 while rendering correctly. That\nwas ADR-0019''s fallback working as designed — GitHub Pages does no\nrewriting, so a client-side route with no file gets 404.html, which is a\ncopy of index.html. Humans see the right page; crawlers, uptime monitors\nand link checkers see a broken site. There is no fix inside Pages, since\nrewrites are exactly the capability it lacks.\n\nVercel, one project, with a catch-all rewrite to index.html. Vercel\nchecks the filesystem first, so assets and each remote''s mf-manifest.json\nstill serve directly and only the shell''s own routes fall through — now\n200. The /remotes/<name>/ layout from ADR-0019 is unchanged; that\ndecision was about a path collision, not about Pages.\n\nSingle project rather than one per remote: a project per app is closer to\nthe architecture and would exercise origin-guard and the CSP against real\ncross-origin loads, but it triples the setup before an evaluator sees\nanything. Deferred deliberately, and the registry already supports it.\n\nThe assemble moved from CI steps into scripts/build-site.ts, because\nVercel''s build is one command and expressing the layout twice is two\nplaces to drift. basePath is gone — a Vercel project serves from the\ndomain root.\n\nPackages retargeted from GitHub Packages to public npm. The old config\ncould not have worked: GitHub Packages requires the scope to match the\nrepo owner, and these are @enterprise-mfe under rodvieira. Public npm\nalso means an adopter installs with no token and no .npmrc at all.\nChangeset included for the first real release, 0.0.0 -> 0.1.0.\n\nFound while doing it: `pnpm lint` hung after a site build, because\nbiome''s ignore list covered dist/ but not the new _site/ and it was\nwalking every generated bundle. Added there and to the eject''s walker.","tree":{"sha":"0dd1f2a47df7035011b32ebaf8b699e4382fd146","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/git/trees/0dd1f2a47df7035011b32ebaf8b699e4382fd146"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/git/commits/4a9db63c71a2e5f167c04a7b837ad70702287e76","verification":{"payload":"tree 0dd1f2a47df7035011b32ebaf8b699e4382fd146\nparent c531f53afdd8baf2ccfad949193ab1410e088884\nauthor Rodrigo Vieira <rodrigodenizads@gmail.com> 1787008134 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787008134 -0300\n\nfeat(repo): move the reference deploy to Vercel, publish to npm (ADR-0026) (#50)\n\nA browser check of production found what curl smoke tests had missed:\n/dashboard and /admin returned HTTP 404 while rendering correctly. That\nwas ADR-0019''s fallback working as designed — GitHub Pages does no\nrewriting, so a client-side route with no file gets 404.html, which is a\ncopy of index.html. Humans see the right page; crawlers, uptime monitors\nand link checkers see a broken site. There is no fix inside Pages, since\nrewrites are exactly the capability it lacks.\n\nVercel, one project, with a catch-all rewrite to index.html. Vercel\nchecks the filesystem first, so assets and each remote''s mf-manifest.json\nstill serve directly and only the shell''s own routes fall through — now\n200. The /remotes/<name>/ layout from ADR-0019 is unchanged; that\ndecision was about a path collision, not about Pages.\n\nSingle project rather than one per remote: a project per app is closer to\nthe architecture and would exercise origin-guard and the CSP against real\ncross-origin loads, but it triples the setup before an evaluator sees\nanything. Deferred deliberately, and the registry already supports it.\n\nThe assemble moved from CI steps into scripts/build-site.ts, because\nVercel''s build is one command and expressing the layout twice is two\nplaces to drift. basePath is gone — a Vercel project serves from the\ndomain root.\n\nPackages retargeted from GitHub Packages to public npm. The old config\ncould not have worked: GitHub Packages requires the scope to match the\nrepo owner, and these are @enterprise-mfe under rodvieira. Public npm\nalso means an adopter installs with no token and no .npmrc at all.\nChangeset included for the first real release, 0.0.0 -> 0.1.0.\n\nFound while doing it: `pnpm lint` hung after a site build, because\nbiome''s ignore list covered dist/ but not the new _site/ and it was\nwalking every generated bundle. Added there and to the eject''s walker.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqg5SGCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAOGIQALCJPc3k9mdGEvh2zCiMBGZz\ngmEJxEMTgCPjCeT2UacsfUwn4sPA5qVX2sCmQddVdxalXnGwT+WOPpfpURMFZFko\n8sOf3DmHay2iRJFQvEqjuEtPVhXUDhUeqjdZqZFU6MqCbYny3sdDIp7KijHtR/aQ\n2Q/HqJZ9f0E++JHY5IWQr8FRu6/3jOlaR60vHlkxQll2R7GhEvy5VEN488HHnNc5\ntcQVf9ns1ED8HY2MvJBYLBT1XsXavBqGq78tfFYNVbX7Scv7jgH3IJDnTPD5jEt4\n8i5GkdJ/g1qoVqsXCPjo5PRTLhSGodSMANnEL9h8cgEcrD5/joAEq6emFkoRrT58\nbIosjEv+xICNO/Uc3p3woA5Z3+SBqb3wWAJwvunC7t4GLIfq5G6vUxWa9AtM1GNl\nBzzX1jOzY1TDnRZfHaOhW61o2LZUkeSPGrarSG1HfsG5yf8JIZgc8OBmieGDoOC3\nFgAAlqx/FltZlsryEqtCvWUYUCosNZa/RvMH2a6I3589UOiBxui/FHLMbRt3YEdO\nQ/+Wa/ae27Nn3/YW8DpSFT8fd7NA+z2+Y0PZraOkeLzP/VVeyNBFuCPIKRcGBadi\npip9UNY25E6gt/y3cPGTLqSMJqiKEuH3d/3DQmp1Yzj/YcFeH7hONLTZ8EXfr4fQ\n37DfeO7dWxS7vZ6LNB8B\n=2lNf\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-17T23:08:54Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url