cy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rodvieira","id":35712292,"login":"rodvieira","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1NzEyMjky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commits/6f7768918b3a92cc0d37fb60f1f4e1277e800e88/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-14T01:24:51Z","email":"rodrigodenizads@gmail.com","name":"Rodrigo Vieira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-14T01:24:51Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs(repo): make shipped comments self-contained (#48)\n\n61 references to this project''s own build process were embedded in\nshipped source across 35 files — FR-012, research D3, US2 scenario 1,\nsprint numbers, specs/ paths. They resolve to specs/, which is not\nsomething a reader has open, and which an adopter who ran `pnpm eject`\ndoes not have at all: the eject deletes it. So the comment that was\nsupposed to explain the code pointed at nothing.\n\nMost were pure citations trailing a sentence that already carried the\nexplanation, and are simply gone. The rest were load-bearing — the spec\nid *was* the explanation — and are rewritten to say the thing directly:\n\"FR-005: no configuration required to start\" became \"No configuration\nrequired to start: dev is the default\". Two now link an ADR instead,\nwhich is public and permanent.\n\nReviewing the diff caught two places where deleting a parenthetical left\norphaned punctuation mid-sentence, including a comment that had become\njust \"*.\". Both fixed.\n\nAdds the editorial rule to CLAUDE.md so this does not grow back. Tests\nare deliberately left alone: they are not shipped, and citing a scenario\nis useful there.","tree":{"sha":"dc23d055aab0bff8f7e92ab3dcc88bc196f5e546","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/git/trees/dc23d055aab0bff8f7e92ab3dcc88bc196f5e546"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/git/commits/6f7768918b3a92cc0d37fb60f1f4e1277e800e88","verification":{"payload":"tree dc23d055aab0bff8f7e92ab3dcc88bc196f5e546\nparent 71d708f20da8a84eeb33fd4928d77e2458e31058\nauthor Rodrigo Vieira <rodrigodenizads@gmail.com> 1786670691 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786670691 -0300\n\ndocs(repo): make shipped comments self-contained (#48)\n\n61 references to this project''s own build process were embedded in\nshipped source across 35 files — FR-012, research D3, US2 scenario 1,\nsprint numbers, specs/ paths. They resolve to specs/, which is not\nsomething a reader has open, and which an adopter who ran `pnpm eject`\ndoes not have at all: the eject deletes it. So the comment that was\nsupposed to explain the code pointed at nothing.\n\nMost were pure citations trailing a sentence that already carried the\nexplanation, and are simply gone. The rest were load-bearing — the spec\nid *was* the explanation — and are rewritten to say the thing directly:\n\"FR-005: no configuration required to start\" became \"No configuration\nrequired to start: dev is the default\". Two now link an ADR instead,\nwhich is public and permanent.\n\nReviewing the diff caught two places where deleting a parenthetical left\norphaned punctuation mid-sentence, including a comment that had become\njust \"*.\". Both fixed.\n\nAdds the editorial rule to CLAUDE.md so this does not grow back. Tests\nare deliberately left alone: they are not shipped, and citing a scenario\nis useful there.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqfm5jCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAO7sQAAqKj/SNr6qmVOQwqzKx7n+S\nU+c67aLo1I4zghwtRfD18oShfb1wSCBvoVt3dQo3zEsCLnXLyC3TCombWOuJAl8i\nm3DBkPf3cFl/Cvv2CUt8sJjNm4ytQCuo3/GlkFkuGsMPLZDNoaQLoljKjuYbGmN6\n6SsVEi/XR1KcjcpSSF6+wiVoD4fbgk5ZYmq9rARc2D9yCKMv9Xo4Cvlv7yOniknL\nH/lEIs88xL9h5BSgKP+GWXid15tib5+1WPTEKh6jQ5eq3xB8dDt39XVOHtVKFR1k\nZjauAhqpS5vcY+FgjGss5EuAOCMKItkXfshHAeDdewbncrZw+0bbRVdSFaXhyncN\nZDstSF7IZZwk9mST/w+RQ/V8NP/njXZPJd9Xa7vkddnEQ8yzh+K8aCg2aCKaUBsR\n4EDyRJvmNEsTRUvNNZO/xtuYPcd1OgwKyqm78sL0+rZyrXepWRSNnMGgQrVMr/XG\ng18+R2YJXpdiGMqXmaeqwsGnEiupQx/yr87aw9CTWsW2+w/75caidYAf3toC8wK1\nxpRVfYxsEEllTLmLV+en2rA/2BOdt8HdRMY3vidkNdqRav5PTxwgRCWXLadSG756\nwvPgUZts5zc80mIm+crdyH1zGjTe+KRAGmF2nH7Y/mh6VQtpApRDRvP8nbfszHek\nLFQp5E++O8PJam1cpcIu\n=4QIx\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-14T01:24:58Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commit/6f7768918b3a92cc0d37fb60f1f4e1277e800e88","node_id":"C_kwDOTrv84doAKDZmNzc2ODkxOGIzYTkyY2MwZDM3ZmI2MGYxZjRlMTI3N2U4MDBlODg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commit/71d708f20da8a84eeb33fd4928d77e2458e31058","sha":"71d708f20da8a84eeb33fd4928d77e2458e31058","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commits/71d708f20da8a84eeb33fd4928d77e2458e31058"}],"sha":"6f7768918b3a92cc0d37fb60f1f4e1277e800e88","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commits/6f7768918b3a92cc0d37fb60f1f4e1277e800e88"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35712292?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rodvieira","id":35712292,"login":"rodvieira","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1NzEyMjky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commits/71d708f20da8a84eeb33fd4928d77e2458e31058/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-14T01:16:42Z","email":"rodrigodenizads@gmail.com","name":"Rodrigo Vieira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-14T01:16:42Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: validate cross-tab event payloads (ADR-0025) (#47)\n\n* feat(event-bus): validate cross-tab payloads at the receiving edge (ADR-0025)\n\nSame-tab delivery needs no runtime check: publisher and subscriber are one\nbuild, compiled together. Cross-tab delivery is different, for a reason\nspecific to this architecture rather than generic paranoia — two tabs can\nbe running two independently-deployed builds of the same remote, which is\nthe premise of the whole project. A tab left open on last week''s admin\nposts exactly the payload last week''s EventMap described, and today''s\ndashboard hands it to a subscriber typed as valid.\n\nOne type-guard per topic now runs at the channel edge. Failures are\ndropped with a warning, never thrown: a newer tab publishing a topic this\nbuild has never heard of is the expected state during a rollout, and there\nis no caller to catch a throw inside an event listener anyway.\n\nHand-written rather than a schema library — one topic, ten lines, and this\nproject requires a justification per dependency. EventValidators is a\nmapped type over EventMap, so adding a topic without its validator is a\ntype error rather than a silently unvalidated one. The role check reads\nshared-types'' own ROLE_PERMISSIONS so it cannot drift from the type.\n\nThe security framing is the weaker one and the ADR says so:\nBroadcastChannel is same-origin, and a script that can post to it can\nalready do worse. Version skew is the real reason.\n\n* test(event-bus): make cross-tab assertions deterministic, not timed\n\nCI caught what a local run had hidden: the new cross-tab tests were\nracy. They waited setTimeout(0) for BroadcastChannel delivery, which is\nasynchronous and, under CI load, arbitrarily slower than that — so one\ntest''s message arrived while the next was running. The failure was\nunmistakable once seen: the \"drops an invalid payload\" test received the\n*valid* payload from the test before it.\n\nDelivery preserves order, so the wait is now a sentinel: post a known-good\npayload after the message under test and wait for that. When the sentinel\narrives, the message under test has already been handled, whether it was\ndelivered or dropped. Subscribers filter sentinels out of what they\nrecord, so a negative assertion stays a real negative.\n\nVerified 6x isolated, 3x full suite, and once under CPU load: 240 stable.","tree":{"sha":"fc6f4fc9c8603e67cdcb4f0d915a28deceb7e5e6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/git/trees/fc6f4fc9c8603e67cdcb4f0d915a28deceb7e5e6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/git/commits/71d708f20da8a84eeb33fd4928d77e2458e31058","verification":{"payload":"tree fc6f4fc9c8603e67cdcb4f0d915a28deceb7e5e6\nparent 3d18352bdd70ca17875f41c2407444aa7711fc54\nauthor Rodrigo Vieira <rodrigodenizads@gmail.com> 1786670202 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786670202 -0300\n\nfeat: validate cross-tab event payloads (ADR-0025) (#47)\n\n* feat(event-bus): validate cross-tab payloads at the receiving edge (ADR-0025)\n\nSame-tab delivery needs no runtime check: publisher and subscriber are one\nbuild, compiled together. Cross-tab delivery is different, for a reason\nspecific to this architecture rather than generic paranoia — two tabs can\nbe running two independently-deployed builds of the same remote, which is\nthe premise of the whole project. A tab left open on last week''s admin\nposts exactly the payload last week''s EventMap described, and today''s\ndashboard hands it to a subscriber typed as valid.\n\nOne type-guard per topic now runs at the channel edge. Failures are\ndropped with a warning, never thrown: a newer tab publishing a topic this\nbuild has never heard of is the expected state during a rollout, and there\nis no caller to catch a throw inside an event listener anyway.\n\nHand-written rather than a schema library — one topic, ten lines, and this\nproject requires a justification per dependency. EventValidators is a\nmapped type over EventMap, so adding a topic without its validator is a\ntype error rather than a silently unvalidated one. The role check reads\nshared-types'' own ROLE_PERMISSIONS so it cannot drift from the type.\n\nThe security framing is the weaker one and the ADR says so:\nBroadcastChannel is same-origin, and a script that can post to it can\nalready do worse. Version skew is the real reason.\n\n* test(event-bus): make cross-tab assertions deterministic, not timed\n\nCI caught what a local run had hidden: the new cross-tab tests were\nracy. They waited setTimeout(0) for BroadcastChannel delivery, which is\nasynchronous and, under CI load, arbitrarily slower than that — so one\ntest''s message arrived while the next was running. The failure was\nunmistakable once seen: the \"drops an invalid payload\" test received the\n*valid* payload from the test before it.\n\nDelivery preserves order, so the wait is now a sentinel: post a known-good\npayload after the message under test and wait for that. When the sentinel\narrives, the message under test has already been handled, whether it was\ndelivered or dropped. Subscribers filter sentinels out of what they\nrecord, so a negative assertion stays a real negative.\n\nVerified 6x isolated, 3x full suite, and once under CPU load: 240 stable.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqfmx6CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA4+IQAAacwMFblvNrOeTAGNFhkIX9\n+AKGYay6AWChyitcroCPnOO9PnczXh7eJj0RvjT6SsXzE4raRDYoVHYCgY4rmroH\ngfwoJ8OcbY9A5TLawPvc8q9ccEc0u/pF8u8osm8KTC8S290C9KJe7vjJJWVx72z0\nsp+y5FPk8p5AAmSrOdxGaxXziImAzRhZY/evdmGWBEYb76y0YAUHYyb87U/pwq2X\n+bZ5xo+RF8WHn1UG4Ix7vHB21Sgiuzk2jvyDfVASvtlmRAeWQCbRuoP3JjDaLd/e\n4ABcalvF+PFAae904Wm+c6l6aWWlZ7BgyGqP5qBo7cVslfTficd7Y86RDTTLfm90\n6L/QfI9Rx0cR8n6ufH20DunVCyg30XriGewFaxrCBr4WcGg61xXDwbpHijysayIW\nRLmonISdMg8RgFSJaIFZsnSIuUnEvVVNzuqi4cKJ4jrmwpMcD8/ztl8CIXUcdzdT\nOfRlfAuPUcy766wb3MrLUBLbcmYs9/9MUo+Zeb7CtBD08S4XrMdBKNy/V65wYIiA\nF+o8yKRNfTSbytGdhSoQ7qvjR5hCK/DxbpFpSBF50IPhJTLVJ8kCPiK7tSrRFk9e\nPdOMZ/BUZB/0bX+ZVQDLiKhEviLxy5yK44qf5kzdoIO9IxGMRR9IS9FhyOVtJCOC\nYQdFyNUOy5EHGZUQQbSD\n=w1Sa\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-14T01:16:50Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commit/71d708f20da8a84eeb33fd4928d77e2458e31058","node_id":"C_kwDOTrv84doAKDcxZDcwOGYyMGRhOGE4NGVlYjMzZmQ0OTI4ZDc3ZTI0NThlMzEwNTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commit/3d18352bdd70ca17875f41c2407444aa7711fc54","sha":"3d18352bdd70ca17875f41c2407444aa7711fc54","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commits/3d18352bdd70ca17875f41c2407444aa7711fc54"}],"sha":"71d708f20da8a84eeb33fd4928d77e2458e31058","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commits/71d708f20da8a84eeb33fd4928d77e2458e31058"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35712292?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rodvieira","id":35712292,"login":"rodvieira","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1NzEyMjky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commits/3d18352bdd70ca17875f41c2407444aa7711fc54/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-14T01:05:15Z","email":"rodrigodenizads@gmail.com","name":"Rodrigo Vieira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-14T01:05:15Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(repo): guard Tailwind version agreement across apps (ADR-0024) (#46)\n\nNothing in this repo had ever stated a position on CSS across remotes —\nthe most visible gap in the ADR set. Measured against a real build: each\napp emits ~24KB of CSS and its own Tailwind preflight, so a composed page\ncarries ~72KB where 24KB would do, applying the reset three times.\n\nToday that is waste, not breakage — all three declare ^4.3.3, so the\nresets are byte-identical and re-applying them is idempotent. The hazard\nis what independent deployment makes possible: dashboard on 4.3 and admin\non 4.5, shipped weeks apart. Their preflights differ, whichever loads\nlast wins, and base elements across the whole page quietly restyle with\nnothing failing and nothing to grep for.\n\nSo the version is guarded rather than the CSS isolated. tailwindcss and\n@tailwindcss/postcss join check-shared-deps — build-time dependencies in\na list that held only runtime-shared ones, for exactly the same reason\nthe others are there.\n\nDeliberately NOT done: preflight only in the shell. That breaks ADR-0007\n— a remote with no reset of its own renders correctly only inside this\nshell, turning an independent app into a fragment that merely looks\nindependent. CSS @layer was considered too: it fixes precedence, which\nhas not been a problem here, and not duplication, which is.","tree":{"sha":"afd58bba722e876681ffa831754c7ff67c575bbd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/git/trees/afd58bba722e876681ffa831754c7ff67c575bbd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/git/commits/3d18352bdd70ca17875f41c2407444aa7711fc54","verification":{"payload":"tree afd58bba722e876681ffa831754c7ff67c575bbd\nparent bf3492ef9fb78e8a801e19a93c2f132284459cbc\nauthor Rodrigo Vieira <rodrigodenizads@gmail.com> 1786669515 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786669515 -0300\n\nfix(repo): guard Tailwind version agreement across apps (ADR-0024) (#46)\n\nNothing in this repo had ever stated a position on CSS across remotes —\nthe most visible gap in the ADR set. Measured against a real build: each\napp emits ~24KB of CSS and its own Tailwind preflight, so a composed page\ncarries ~72KB where 24KB would do, applying the reset three times.\n\nToday that is waste, not breakage — all three declare ^4.3.3, so the\nresets are byte-identical and re-applying them is idempotent. The hazard\nis what independent deployment makes possible: dashboard on 4.3 and admin\non 4.5, shipped weeks apart. Their preflights differ, whichever loads\nlast wins, and base elements across the whole page quietly restyle with\nnothing failing and nothing to grep for.\n\nSo the version is guarded rather than the CSS isolated. tailwindcss and\n@tailwindcss/postcss join check-shared-deps — build-time dependencies in\na list that held only runtime-shared ones, for exactly the same reason\nthe others are there.\n\nDeliberately NOT done: preflight only in the shell. That breaks ADR-0007\n— a remote with no reset of its own renders correctly only inside this\nshell, turning an independent app into a fragment that merely looks\nindependent. CSS @layer was considered too: it fixes precedence, which\nhas not been a problem here, and not duplication, which is.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqfmnLCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAtsYQABrXz9f2jymJmUC3JAL5bb+n\naZrgxhTzLaCwrggZ0Z0RcBFu5yXsV8298Vb7Jq27opZh07WVfR090AnM/mf89BB7\nxDtZn3RHydjWyypmVc1RNAfmGgZChZNmXlNLIXcYj0/b5YMX43CIDsuK/STD7d0M\nDmtq5Dm+Ef6VpkIbr+R0UC1ynrYqo9pUY2Vq/k9lcqxCwUrUJhgxDa3cR7Kx18qI\n/2VMcqJdzSYl4CYLI/pE/109OalJ4E3Ykr0MhaFLEdDaRKFwTeNOQiUqr0uexiJJ\nDw2VUD/o0MsXcQvMj4VgrUsxsyUfPHRmeg7MpYLbTQYDMruT+hQ0+P3Rv1ycThYd\nP0rpYHbWzryo+1zDcmDO6q+j3IJfF1lZoTTWOlqUGP6LGfqwcPl1qKAtTfAgvfGG\nOeiVvIc4ClyvW4Moix9qnv6PxSzhjccBt/hJ4fy9OPP3wjGffkVO6ClPzIqQ0mGZ\n6gsFfVVoiBEzvZQ8zCUAXqoXs1nFUcRzg+UvT4dqFJHisz61HH0zkmsAh2d3SDBF\nxOLyLtf20yagfFWOu6gOvowfN5UKw79Z8A3oltiB07B/4JywssjOvHzMNK7Y16lZ\n3KzQvWimICdRSYS6ujXpXnU9h57fKYHc0Imh8oXfUqlyUIHPg3g/ievsGKDJh8m8\nyHVtZ6zh8j6uj6H7uHKz\n=jP91\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-14T01:05:24Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commit/3d18352bdd70ca17875f41c2407444aa7711fc54","node_id":"C_kwDOTrv84doAKDNkMTgzNTJiZGQ3MGNhMTc4NzVmNDFjMjQwNzQ0NGFhNzcxMWZjNTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commit/bf3492ef9fb78e8a801e19a93c2f132284459cbc","sha":"bf3492ef9fb78e8a801e19a93c2f132284459cbc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commits/bf3492ef9fb78e8a801e19a93c2f132284459cbc"}],"sha":"3d18352bdd70ca17875f41c2407444aa7711fc54","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commits/3d18352bdd70ca17875f41c2407444aa7711fc54"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35712292?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rodvieira","id":35712292,"login":"rodvieira","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1NzEyMjky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commits/bf3492ef9fb78e8a801e19a93c2f132284459cbc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-14T00:58:26Z","email":"rodrigodenizads@gmail.com","name":"Rodrigo Vieira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-14T00:58:26Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(telemetry): observability contract with a console default (ADR-0023) (#45)\n\nRemoteBoundary has exposed onError since sprint 1 so the package would\nnot depend on a telemetry vendor. Nothing ever consumed it — the only\ncaller was its own test — and useRemote timed nothing. So the questions a\nhost is uniquely able to answer went unanswerable: which remote failed,\nhow long loads take, and, since ADR-0022 put a version in the registry,\nwhich build introduced a regression.\n\npackages/telemetry ships the interface and a console sink, not a vendor\nintegration — the same decision ADR-0009 made about identity, for the\nsame reason. Four events, keeping load failure and render crash apart:\nthey have different causes and different owners, and collapsing them is\nwhat makes a dashboard useless during an incident.\n\nThe instrumentation wraps the loader in the shell''s RemoteRegion rather\nthan living in federation-utils, which depends on nothing on purpose.\n\nTwo guarantees the provider enforces so adopters need not: a throwing\nimplementation is swallowed (telemetry must not break what it observes),\nand useTelemetry falls back to the console outside a provider, so a\nremote rendered standalone still works.\n\nJoins the singleton check and the shell''s MF shared config per\nconstitution Principle III — two copies would mean a remote reporting\ninto its own default while the host believes everything reaches its\nvendor, a gap that looks exactly like healthy silence.\n\nAlso relaxes the generator''s cross-check to a subset: the two singleton\nlists answer different questions, and telemetry is one a remote opts into\nrather than one every generated remote needs.","tree":{"sha":"a1cd0833ca5d4aab0aa500a6518a832678bc8724","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/git/trees/a1cd0833ca5d4aab0aa500a6518a832678bc8724"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/git/commits/bf3492ef9fb78e8a801e19a93c2f132284459cbc","verification":{"payload":"tree a1cd0833ca5d4aab0aa500a6518a832678bc8724\nparent 3c1ca3dc0702265ea5e46ebf0ed1ba116dd4eb06\nauthor Rodrigo Vieira <rodrigodenizads@gmail.com> 1786669106 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786669106 -0300\n\nfeat(telemetry): observability contract with a console default (ADR-0023) (#45)\n\nRemoteBoundary has exposed onError since sprint 1 so the package would\nnot depend on a telemetry vendor. Nothing ever consumed it — the only\ncaller was its own test — and useRemote timed nothing. So the questions a\nhost is uniquely able to answer went unanswerable: which remote failed,\nhow long loads take, and, since ADR-0022 put a version in the registry,\nwhich build introduced a regression.\n\npackages/telemetry ships the interface and a console sink, not a vendor\nintegration — the same decision ADR-0009 made about identity, for the\nsame reason. Four events, keeping load failure and render crash apart:\nthey have different causes and different owners, and collapsing them is\nwhat makes a dashboard useless during an incident.\n\nThe instrumentation wraps the loader in the shell''s RemoteRegion rather\nthan living in federation-utils, which depends on nothing on purpose.\n\nTwo guarantees the provider enforces so adopters need not: a throwing\nimplementation is swallowed (telemetry must not break what it observes),\nand useTelemetry falls back to the console outside a provider, so a\nremote rendered standalone still works.\n\nJoins the singleton check and the shell''s MF shared config per\nconstitution Principle III — two copies would mean a remote reporting\ninto its own default while the host believes everything reaches its\nvendor, a gap that looks exactly like healthy silence.\n\nAlso relaxes the generator''s cross-check to a subset: the two singleton\nlists answer different questions, and telemetry is one a remote opts into\nrather than one every generated remote needs.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqfmgyCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjgUQACLZ4/ICdCKY1vipVA0n2h+N\nqSHT/rXBpbg72H65kiiZ3FiqYVY6caUQn6fOQ1/CJoFEvU3HAJEjrZayIPNxYOi6\ndUgJxsLu3RKrycLdN7IfcLJ31liGqe3Run1Qay4dNofBInAJITgkgdhX5fWjiBHU\nZdpmNk9lAw10CX6ljjxpPy6KHdBrXTMNQ083vizHsjx9E8dF/zwviOh4DpI0VDUl\nIXk/eIn8RRC8sRTEupJDOFzY7GpW5VtORM4r41Qsl5pTFh3gN519QQYZit8dyqFa\nlF4AKqYqErayTaQdHtnWAEYtqKBbjU8Mv7QVuNF3uQiyU4/yYiEbDSffPtI1IvUG\n0kIsXsdHNw+FNAgOH1a8X9084uxmnhRvuNQMu5eygSpTsQKTGvXa6WNXYC3Z7fHA\nQ39HpbghETRGLXfL//XfMRVchgyHPLu9btCTYr+N5RsDUCUKV7vk+XrimDp87DLA\n0zlxps7cRm96hU/E6oJTHdK0BHB5gkPNrCSo7G3NR8otu2ZwIc/B65tjx9+Vn15s\nAn6g2tlRLtUVQfXH4azgRXh97DqDg2GqbKuExbkJF6SlOQhhaK0+GSvhMc6qHngf\nHA+p+8e03W8jBq96w0g7qStDhNWZsC8JH0ePuhnSBl82r0SBlMxFCtwYEN9348nX\nMN/26Ks6Yjk9sgwtBfCG\n=8RmW\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-14T00:58:34Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commit/bf3492ef9fb78e8a801e19a93c2f132284459cbc","node_id":"C_kwDOTrv84doAKGJmMzQ5MmVmOWZiNzhlOGE4MDFlMTlhOTNjMmYxMzIyODQ0NTljYmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commit/3c1ca3dc0702265ea5e46ebf0ed1ba116dd4eb06","sha":"3c1ca3dc0702265ea5e46ebf0ed1ba116dd4eb06","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commits/3c1ca3dc0702265ea5e46ebf0ed1ba116dd4eb06"}],"sha":"bf3492ef9fb78e8a801e19a93c2f132284459cbc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commits/bf3492ef9fb78e8a801e19a93c2f132284459cbc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35712292?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rodvieira","id":35712292,"login":"rodvieira","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1NzEyMjky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commits/3c1ca3dc0702265ea5e46ebf0ed1ba116dd4eb06/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-14T00:45:04Z","email":"rodrigodenizads@gmail.com","name":"Rodrigo Vieira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-14T00:45:04Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(shell): let a registry entry state which build it points at (ADR-0022) (#44)\n\nThe registry already made \"switch environment = switch a file\" true, but\nnever recorded which build of a remote an entry pointed at. That left the\nmain operational reason to adopt micro-frontends on the table: rolling\none remote back without touching the others. It also left incident\nresponse reconstructing versions from URLs.\n\nRemoteRegistration gains an optional `version`, and how-to-deploy.md\ndocuments the immutable-versioned-path convention that gives it meaning —\nrollback becomes editing one string and redeploying the registry JSON,\nbecause the previous build was never overwritten.\n\nOptional on purpose: a remote on a mutable path has no version to state,\nand a required field would be filled with a lie. Never resolved by the\nhost either — `entry` alone decides what loads; comparing versions would\nmake the registry a resolver and reintroduce the coupling ADR-0012\nremoved. But a present-and-unusable version (null, \"\") is rejected at\nstartup: that shape is a pipeline substituting a value it failed to\ncompute, and dropping it silently loses the one fact worth having.\n\nDiagnostics now read `dashboard@1.4.2` via describeRemote().","tree":{"sha":"5e7770ef605d4e4dc415d2153c116ec2f3a23641","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/git/trees/5e7770ef605d4e4dc415d2153c116ec2f3a23641"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/git/commits/3c1ca3dc0702265ea5e46ebf0ed1ba116dd4eb06","verification":{"payload":"tree 5e7770ef605d4e4dc415d2153c116ec2f3a23641\nparent 4a9f903f8daaa0dfaad3c63fea87838fa9766271\nauthor Rodrigo Vieira <rodrigodenizads@gmail.com> 1786668304 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786668304 -0300\n\nfeat(shell): let a registry entry state which build it points at (ADR-0022) (#44)\n\nThe registry already made \"switch environment = switch a file\" true, but\nnever recorded which build of a remote an entry pointed at. That left the\nmain operational reason to adopt micro-frontends on the table: rolling\none remote back without touching the others. It also left incident\nresponse reconstructing versions from URLs.\n\nRemoteRegistration gains an optional `version`, and how-to-deploy.md\ndocuments the immutable-versioned-path convention that gives it meaning —\nrollback becomes editing one string and redeploying the registry JSON,\nbecause the previous build was never overwritten.\n\nOptional on purpose: a remote on a mutable path has no version to state,\nand a required field would be filled with a lie. Never resolved by the\nhost either — `entry` alone decides what loads; comparing versions would\nmake the registry a resolver and reintroduce the coupling ADR-0012\nremoved. But a present-and-unusable version (null, \"\") is rejected at\nstartup: that shape is a pipeline substituting a value it failed to\ncompute, and dropping it silently loses the one fact worth having.\n\nDiagnostics now read `dashboard@1.4.2` via describeRemote().","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqfmURCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAbv8QACHbU4EB4064l5rhHs+a3ZR7\nSxSBeDG5oMUFs28OlPT+6WEZ9VecfSFVkPy9PMSK/tQt9WTs4WI2PGL3xSfPTEoc\nYBKF2HtWj50lFyTArulsZByFIj6EyC8fSGj42AUKPrQkRyHY/BP8lATwFzl56AQv\nBRyElR5XZgDLtDfSTd2DYh4lqPrNydY0u+3b/b1zrCjmPfkprCya6yaCaLsbYhoY\nYwNdd7tllxIzuhC+N8sL8/yi12UhZYnAqBQlQShhTvgMhzh9klwIUVEIGysgHkab\n39N0Or+pkb4jDTAE3KxnvNl/bUIVVtUM6tYrIKZh3orpKG6FwhtV8kIcJ841nktM\nI1M04Hb8silhIUxaXM3DCQRN06oyPSNNo0g4enO9K0XHyAojA9+NxKmh2PL4VG7b\nAOW