e07b4a0b786a7b601b2bb7ee8e515e68","sha":"558b76f1e07b4a0b786a7b601b2bb7ee8e515e68","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commits/558b76f1e07b4a0b786a7b601b2bb7ee8e515e68"}],"sha":"688a987a428b2d57af106b91e6eb78ea322adb3f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commits/688a987a428b2d57af106b91e6eb78ea322adb3f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35712292?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rodvieira","id":35712292,"login":"rodvieira","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1NzEyMjky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commits/558b76f1e07b4a0b786a7b601b2bb7ee8e515e68/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-11T01:29:45Z","email":"rodrigodenizads@gmail.com","name":"Rodrigo Vieira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-11T01:29:45Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Sprint 9: launch prep — README, technical post draft, deploy guide (#29)\n\n* docs(repo): specify, plan, and break down sprint 9 — launch prep\n\nPrepares the three launch artifacts that live in version control:\nREADME, a technical post draft, and deploy documentation. Scoped\ndown (confirmed with the user) to exclude the four Portfolio DoD\nitems that require real external action outside this repo — the\nactual production deploy, recording the demo GIF, pinning the\nrepository, and publishing the post externally.\n\n* docs(repo): rewrite README for launch (T001-T003)\n\nReplaces the \"under active development\" stub with real content:\nwhat the project is, why it exists (the gap in existing\nmicro-frontend starters), what''s actually running (shell, two real\nremotes, the generator, guard rails), a working quick start, and\nlinks to the blueprint, architecture reference, and ADRs.\n\nOne clearly-marked \"Demo & live URLs\" section notes both are pending\na real deploy and recording — the maintainer''s own next action, not\nscattered placeholders across the file.\n\n* docs(repo): draft the exposed/internal boundary technical post (T004-T006)\n\nThe one technical post the blueprint names explicitly, as a\ncomplete, publication-ready draft — the maintainer''s remaining work\nis picking a platform, not writing it.\n\nBuilt on two real \"got this wrong the first time\" stories, both\nverified word-for-word against source rather than paraphrased from\nmemory: the dependency-cruiser backreference bug that only surfaced\nonce a second real app existed to trip it (.dependency-cruiser.js''s\nown \"issue #2\" comment), and the Tailwind chunk-loading gotcha found\nbuilding apps/dashboard''s activity chart (a remote''s exposed entry\nmust import its own stylesheet directly, since Module Federation\nonly loads the exposed module''s own dependency graph).\n\n* docs(repo): document the real deploy mechanism (T007-T009)\n\nHost-agnostic on purpose: every app builds to static assets with no\nserver-side requirement, and this project has never committed to a\nspecific static host (same reasoning 007-docs-security''s research D1\nalready applied to the CSP being a meta tag, not a header).\n\nDocuments the real FEDERATION_ENV mechanism (verified by actually\nrunning FEDERATION_ENV=production/staging builds and inspecting the\nemitted remotes.json against the claims), what a maintainer updates\nin remotes.<env>.json once a remote has a real URL, and states\nplainly that remotes.staging.json/remotes.production.json currently\nship with empty remotes arrays — a real, current fact, not an\nimplied live deployment.\n\n* docs(repo): drop the technical post draft from version control\n\nPer user direction: content meant for an external post (LinkedIn/blog)\nshouldn''t be committed to this repository. The draft is preserved\noutside git for the maintainer''s own use. README''s \"Learn more\" section\nno longer links to it.","tree":{"sha":"3681f448c0c7ae48e7037a3a9d5c70630e223deb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/git/trees/3681f448c0c7ae48e7037a3a9d5c70630e223deb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/git/commits/558b76f1e07b4a0b786a7b601b2bb7ee8e515e68","verification":{"payload":"tree 3681f448c0c7ae48e7037a3a9d5c70630e223deb\nparent 32792d96d5276a258f4595d9fd7f39c5d53ddb94\nauthor Rodrigo Vieira <rodrigodenizads@gmail.com> 1786411785 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786411785 -0300\n\nSprint 9: launch prep — README, technical post draft, deploy guide (#29)\n\n* docs(repo): specify, plan, and break down sprint 9 — launch prep\n\nPrepares the three launch artifacts that live in version control:\nREADME, a technical post draft, and deploy documentation. Scoped\ndown (confirmed with the user) to exclude the four Portfolio DoD\nitems that require real external action outside this repo — the\nactual production deploy, recording the demo GIF, pinning the\nrepository, and publishing the post externally.\n\n* docs(repo): rewrite README for launch (T001-T003)\n\nReplaces the \"under active development\" stub with real content:\nwhat the project is, why it exists (the gap in existing\nmicro-frontend starters), what''s actually running (shell, two real\nremotes, the generator, guard rails), a working quick start, and\nlinks to the blueprint, architecture reference, and ADRs.\n\nOne clearly-marked \"Demo & live URLs\" section notes both are pending\na real deploy and recording — the maintainer''s own next action, not\nscattered placeholders across the file.\n\n* docs(repo): draft the exposed/internal boundary technical post (T004-T006)\n\nThe one technical post the blueprint names explicitly, as a\ncomplete, publication-ready draft — the maintainer''s remaining work\nis picking a platform, not writing it.\n\nBuilt on two real \"got this wrong the first time\" stories, both\nverified word-for-word against source rather than paraphrased from\nmemory: the dependency-cruiser backreference bug that only surfaced\nonce a second real app existed to trip it (.dependency-cruiser.js''s\nown \"issue #2\" comment), and the Tailwind chunk-loading gotcha found\nbuilding apps/dashboard''s activity chart (a remote''s exposed entry\nmust import its own stylesheet directly, since Module Federation\nonly loads the exposed module''s own dependency graph).\n\n* docs(repo): document the real deploy mechanism (T007-T009)\n\nHost-agnostic on purpose: every app builds to static assets with no\nserver-side requirement, and this project has never committed to a\nspecific static host (same reasoning 007-docs-security''s research D1\nalready applied to the CSP being a meta tag, not a header).\n\nDocuments the real FEDERATION_ENV mechanism (verified by actually\nrunning FEDERATION_ENV=production/staging builds and inspecting the\nemitted remotes.json against the claims), what a maintainer updates\nin remotes.<env>.json once a remote has a real URL, and states\nplainly that remotes.staging.json/remotes.production.json currently\nship with empty remotes arrays — a real, current fact, not an\nimplied live deployment.\n\n* docs(repo): drop the technical post draft from version control\n\nPer user direction: content meant for an external post (LinkedIn/blog)\nshouldn''t be committed to this repository. The draft is preserved\noutside git for the maintainer''s own use. README''s \"Learn more\" section\nno longer links to it.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqensJCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAKrsQAGUh+IDWocQTws/FbYaUavaS\nyVgDz0hMtPdd2KtlT5BaUqfnGI/Ixy4BH1V6/yHdTAporTgHworrrwXzcVkkcdht\nnHOg+Y/07U41B+slkx6AdlJIIcJNfVJXXPTouDBoSE2s4MkjktStUyIpuGZDJTpF\nTaqW1HxHH72KsRIvOQfurj5Y2osI2JMoRp2zrlDMw6NOg4+JpB73qQACACIOuNwo\nTspdvrmPbNBz+i/TcV9WuVpscV3efy42Q5+blSsbMiEiluPfclDWhHs0J2Ibozvp\nOpT3ZXLKJCoqM7M8k54XgIUv1SIxHism/cQWHpYHQZAmq6R0qMEi3yUR6GXgEUTs\ndSCf9F1MXgfvDRj2v5u3KVjUwm5V0WkE2Hr6uG4g6WL5YeTPo0HVRwC6ya4TUUO/\nr3Ky5i7Lrl9Hk/Lb7tpNv+d4Pw7tsNRYBfRZ1AFxh9TzNHH4UJa7w6tQcYl30eE9\nB2485DD1oYbuoeX4rsIKchnNf6NQY5XpqA+fz2D71wqpN3lPDSl7c8DYzbE+DiD5\nyC8KNFHAVCMprq2qxXB0PMWg0BiI88r0Uad5S41y3IWsbpOHA/fyy+/OgnjlubAd\npV2fzUwS8TAF5p9s4RZAqV+01Lb1/ViAUOOpDsu6I7c6I54mRWwR+xvuYsikwWNI\nXlM79TcDu228Ddvi5wj0\n=jNgc\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-11T01:29:49Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url"