.com/users/rodvieira/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commits/99264717511480a188f664bf3eec899f2c8df4e4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-10T22:43:28Z","email":"rodrigodenizads@gmail.com","name":"Rodrigo Vieira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-10T22:43:28Z","email":"rodrigodenizads@gmail.com","name":"Rodrigo Vieira"},"message":"docs(repo): backfill ADR coverage, close sprint 8 (T013-T018)\n\nAudited docs/blueprint.html §2''s ten decisions against\ndocs/decisions/*.md directly rather than assuming coverage (research\nD4): 8/10 already had a 1:1-numbered ADR; 0004 (React 19 + TypeScript\nstrict + Tailwind CSS) and 0005 (pnpm workspaces + Turborepo) sat\nunwritten in the sequence''s own reserved gap. Both backfilled here.\n0015 records this sprint''s own decisions (CSP mechanism, Dependabot,\nOSV-Scanner + Socket) and the audit result.\n\nConfirming CONTRIBUTING.md rather than assuming it satisfied the DoD\nfound two real, stale gaps: its \"Adding a new remote\" section still\ndescribed the pre-generator, hand-copy-only state\n(006-remote-generator has since shipped pnpm turbo gen remote), and\nits security-reporting section still hedged \"until SECURITY.md\nexists\" — that file already existed. Both fixed.\n\ndocs/architecture.md''s origin-allow-list section gains one paragraph\non the CSP mechanism now backing it up at the browser level.","tree":{"sha":"fd1d0913be98b2ee64699a96de004872d168c028","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/git/trees/fd1d0913be98b2ee64699a96de004872d168c028"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/git/commits/99264717511480a188f664bf3eec899f2c8df4e4","verification":{"payload":null,"reaso