l":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commits/246caaf5b633e6608d4b17fc6a0aa1e9bf41f7d3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-06T22:12:50Z","email":"rodrigodenizads@gmail.com","name":"Rodrigo Vieira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-06T22:12:50Z","email":"rodrigodenizads@gmail.com","name":"Rodrigo Vieira"},"message":"docs(admin): specify sprint 5 — the admin remote and packages/event-bus\n\nSpec for apps/admin, the second micro-frontend remote (ADR-0008 build\norder, ADR-0010 domain assignment): a paginated/sorted user table, an\ninvite/edit modal gated by the users:write permission, and role changes.\nShips packages/event-bus alongside it, since ADR-0010''s own proof point\npairs them — a role change in admin must update the dashboard''s \"active\nusers\" KPI live, with neither remote importing the other.\n\nCorrects a stale assumption found while researching scope:\nscripts/check-shared-deps.ts''s comment guessed event-bus arrives in\n\"sprint 6\"; docs/blueprint.html and ADR-0010 place it here, in sprint 5,\npaired with admin. Flagged explicitly in spec.md Dependencies so it isn''t\nmistaken for a real constraint during planning.\n\nOne real ambiguity resolved with a reasoned default: packages/auth''s stub\nalways signs in the same admin-role identity, so the \"permission denied\"\npath is scoped to direct component/unit testing rather than an\ninteractive signed-in test — recorded under Assumptions.\n\nZero [NEEDS CLARIFICATION] markers.","tree":{"sha":"823c386c0e3c1f0775eb7f1f7fc19bfb12569920","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/git/trees/823c386c0e3c1f0775eb7f1f7fc19bfb12569920"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/git/commits/246caaf5b633e6608d4b17f