ite_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commits/ad9f672a8f2a45c2e0bde75c5fe4446c79f41355/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-06T21:55:07Z","email":"rodrigodenizads@gmail.com","name":"Rodrigo Vieira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-06T21:55:07Z","email":"rodrigodenizads@gmail.com","name":"Rodrigo Vieira"},"message":"docs(dashboard): retest boundary and singleton gates against a real second app (US5)\n\npnpm check:boundaries and check:shared-deps both pass cleanly against\napps/dashboard with zero config changes needed — the rules are already\napps/* pattern-based.\n\nRetested issue #6 as planned: a deliberate 3-level relative import from\napps/dashboard into apps/shell/src/internal (one level deeper than the\n2-level case that failed to resolve in sprint 3''s throwaway fixture) was\ncaught correctly by both no-cross-app-relative-imports and\nno-cross-app-reaching-into-internal, then reverted with a clean\ncheck:boundaries run after. Real evidence the original failure was\nfixture/environment-specific, not a standing property of this checkout —\nissue #6 closed with the full result.\n\nAlso proved check:shared-deps catches drift in a second app''s manifest:\na deliberate react-router mismatch in apps/dashboard/package.json failed\nand named both ranges and both manifests, then passed again after revert.","tree":{"sha":"08f99df5e5457ce10f612005484c3487a8a3a1e4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/git/trees/08f99df5e5457ce10f612005484c3487a8a3a1e4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/git/commits/ad9f672a8f2a45c2e0bde75c5fe4446c79f41355","verificat