ira/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodvieira","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/commits/f9bfd7fb6a8866719e6aecdb9342660f049265d2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-04T23:39:59Z","email":"rodrigodenizads@gmail.com","name":"Rodrigo Vieira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-04T23:39:59Z","email":"rodrigodenizads@gmail.com","name":"Rodrigo Vieira"},"message":"docs(shell): add READMEs, architecture doc, and the runtime-registry ADR\n\napps/shell/README.md and packages/federation-utils/README.md; docs/packages.md\nupdated with federation-utils''s real entry (corrected from the blueprint''s\noriginal React.lazy/Suspense sketch to what was actually built — a loader\nfunction, bundler-agnostic by design). docs/architecture.md is new — CLAUDE.md\nreferenced it since the bootstrap commit but it never existed until now.\ndocs/decisions/0012-runtime-registry-fetch.md records research D3.\n\nRunning quickstart.md §1-§7 end to end (T076) found two real bugs, both fixed:\nthe doc''s own --filter shell syntax doesn''t match the actual package name\n(@enterprise-mfe/shell); and turbo.json''s build task didn''t declare\nFEDERATION_ENV as a cache-key input, so a second build with a different\nenvironment silently replayed the first build''s stale remotes.json instead of\nrecomputing — SC-002 would have failed under any warm cache, including CI.","tree":{"sha":"7da11323f61214a59b628fb30a516000ec762877","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/git/trees/7da11323f61214a59b628fb30a516000ec762877"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rodvieira/enterprise-microfrontend-boilerplate/git/commits/f9bfd7fb6a8866719e6aecdb9342660f049265d2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35712